&lt;p&gt;Find out more at: &lt;a id=&quot;menur58p&quot; class=&quot;fui-Link ___1q1shib f2hkw1w f3rmtva f1ewtqcl fyind8e f1k6fduh f1w7gpdv fk6fouc fjoy568 figsok6 f1s184ao f1mk8lai fnbmjn9 f1o700av f13mvf36 f1cmlufx f9n3di6 f1ids18y f1tx3yz7 f1deo86v f1eh06m1 f1iescvh fhgqx19 f1olyrje f1p93eir f1nev41a f1h8hb77 f1lqvz6u f10aw75t fsle3fq f17ae5zn&quot; href=&quot;https://www.agile-robots.com/en/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;https://www.agile-robots.com/en/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/agilerobotsse/mechatronics-and-hardware-test-engineer-munich-bavaria-432664","tags":["Mechatronics Hardware"],"job_types":[],"location":"Munich, Bavaria","created_at":1793645719},{"slug":"cto-co-founder-at-pre-seed-ai-infrastructure-venture-berlin-233950","company_name":"atlantic.vc","title":"CTO & Co-Founder @ Pre-Seed AI Infrastructure Venture, Berlin","description":"<p><em><span style="color:#000000">This is an Atlantic portfolio venture. </span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">About the Venture</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We are building AI infrastructure, with pre-seed funding secured, early customer demand and a product already in production.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We are now looking for a CTO &amp; Co-Founder to shape the company and its technology, scale the product and build the engineering organisation.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">About the Role</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">As </span><strong><span style="color:#000000">CTO &amp; Co-Founder,</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> you will own the technical direction of the company and the team that delivers it. You will lead an existing team of 3 engineers, grow it and set the standards for how it works.<br></span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">We are building an AI-native engineering team from day one, with agentic engineering at the centre of how we write, review and ship code. Coding agents are not an add-on, but the default way we build software.<br></span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">This is a hands-on leadership role. You will stay close to the code while making the technical and organisational decisions that shape the company as it grows.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">What You'll Do</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Lead and develop our existing team of 3 engineers, set high engineering standards and take ownership of what the team ships</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Own technical hiring and build the engineering organisation as the company grows</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Set the technical direction, from architecture and roadmap to build-vs-buy decisions</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Scale and operate reliable AI infrastructure, including APIs, cloud infrastructure, security, GDPR and European data residency</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Stay hands-on, writing code and contributing directly to our core systems</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Build an AI-native engineering culture where coding agents such as Claude Code are central to how the team develops, reviews and ships software</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Design and continuously improve our agentic engineering setup, from harnesses and workflows to orchestrating multiple agents in parallel, evaluating their output and benchmarking what works</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Represent the company technically with customers, in security reviews and in investor conversations<br></span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">About You</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You are an experienced technical leader who still loves to build. You have hired and led engineers, shipped complex systems into production and know how to make good technical decisions under real-world constraints.<br></span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You already work extensively with coding agents and have strong convictions about how AI is changing software engineering. You want to build a team around that approach, and you're excited by the ownership, ambition and uncertainty of becoming a co-founder.</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Proven experience leading, hiring and managing engineering teams, ideally in a startup, whether as a CTO, VP Engineering, Engineering Manager or Tech Lead</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Strong backend and platform foundations, including distributed systems, API design, cloud infrastructure and production systems</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Hands-on experience building and operating AI infrastructure and LLM-powered systems in production</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Extensive daily use of coding agents such as Claude Code, with strong coding fundamentals and the judgement to review and own the quality of their output</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience designing and improving agentic engineering workflows for yourself or a team, including harnesses, multi-agent orchestration and benchmarking, with a clear understanding of their capabilities and limitations</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Nice to Have</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience optimising LLM cost and performance</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Experience serving and operating open-weight models, including GPU and capacity decisions</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Why Join</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Funding is secured, an engineering team is in place and the product is already in production. But many of the most important decisions are still ahead.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">You will have the opportunity to scale the technology, build the team and influence the direction of the company from an early stage, with co-founder equity in the business you help build.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">This is a full-time role, based in our Berlin office 5 days a week, starting as soon as possible.</span></strong></p><p><br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/atlanticvc/cto-co-founder-at-pre-seed-ai-infrastructure-venture-berlin-233950","tags":["Founder & Entrepreneurs in Residence"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Berlin, Berlin, Germany","created_at":1793645485},{"slug":"senior-associate-talent-venture-development-gn-at-atlantic-core-team-berlin-19465","company_name":"atlantic.vc","title":"Senior Associate - Talent & Venture Development (gn) @ Atlantic Core Team, Berlin","description":"<p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Early-Stage Venture Capital &amp; Talent</span></strong></p><p><br><span style="color:#000000">At Atlantic, we back founders in AI, compute, spacetech, and deep tech, often when it's still just a few people and a big idea. What happens next depends less on the idea and more on who joins them: the first engineer who can actually build it, the CTO who scales it, the commercial lead who gets it into the world.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">That's why talent sits at the heart of our Venture Development work. We go out and find those people ourselves, and we help our companies build the organizations around them: how teams are structured, how people are paid, and how they grow.</span><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Why we are looking for you now</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">The breakthroughs we're most excited about will come from people who aren't on anyone's radar yet. We want to find them first and put them where they can have the biggest impact. Talent is scarcer than money in today's VC climate. Promising startup ideas are often replicable. People are not. Together with you, we will:</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Find and win top talent for our portfolio companies, with a focus on senior and leadership hires</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Run searches end to end, from mapping the market to closing the candidate</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Advise our companies on comp, equity, org design, and hiring, and turn what works into playbooks</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Translate business plans into hiring plans, and step in on urgent people topics when needed</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Use AI and automation to make all of this faster and better</span><br></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Your role</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Headhunting is the core of the job. You'll spend your days finding people others miss and convincing them that this is the company worth joining. But you won't just fill roles. You'll sit with our investment team and portfolio CEOs to work out what team a company actually needs, what to pay, and how to structure it, then go and build it. You own your projects and make your own calls. This isn't a standard recruiting gig.</span><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who you will work with</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Our Investment team</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">CEOs and leadership teams across our portfolio, from pre-seed to exit</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">External partners, from recruiters to employment lawyers</span><br></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">What you must have done before</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Placed the top %:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You've found and closed exceptional people, the ones everyone wanted, in fast-growing startups or scale-ups.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Set the bar high:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Your standards for excellence are very, very high, for the people you hire and for your own work.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Ready to do more than search: </span></strong><span style="color:#000000">You want to shape how companies are built, not just fill roles, and you're interested in org design, comp, and equity.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Worked with numbers and concepts:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You're not afraid of numbers, whether comp models or hiring budgets, and you have strong conceptual skills.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Jumped into the unknown:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You're keen to dig into anything new, from employment law to a technology you've never heard of.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Run at a founder's pace:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> You move fast, take ownership, and make your own calls, the way a founder would.</span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Worked internationally:</span></strong><span style="color:#000000"> Fluent English is a must. International work experience and other languages are a big plus.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/atlanticvc/senior-associate-talent-venture-development-gn-at-atlantic-core-team-berlin-19465","tags":["Core Team"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Berlin, Berlin, Germany","created_at":1793645485},{"slug":"werkstudentin-guest-service-munich-167567","company_name":"limehome","title":"Werkstudent:in Guest Service (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Greif mit uns nach den Sternen!<br></strong>Als Werkstudent (m/w/d) Guest Service übernimmst du eine zentrale Rolle in unserem operativen Tagesgeschäft im Hotel Miano by Limehome. Dein Schwerpunkt liegt im morgendlichen Frühstücksservice, Barbetrieb und gleichzeitig bist du im Frontbereich eine zentrale Anlaufstelle mit einem offenen Ohr für alle Anliegen und Wünsche unserer Gäste.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Als ‘Host with heart’ bist du für diese Themen verantwortlich:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="isSelectedEnd"><strong>Frühstücks- &amp; Barservice:</strong> Aufmerksame Betreuung unseres Frühstücksbuffets, Nachbestückung sowie die Zubereitung von klassischen Kaffeespezialitäten, Tees, Heißgetränken und Cocktails</p></li><li><p><strong>Gästebetreuung:</strong> Herzlicher Empfang, Beantwortung von Gästeanfragen (wie Ausflugstipps, Wegbeschreibungen oder Reservierungen) und professionelles Reklamationsmanagement</p></li><li><p><strong>Wohlfühlatmosphäre &amp; Ordnung:</strong> Sicherstellung eines gepflegten, sauberen und einladenden Ambientes im gesamten Loungebereich</p></li><li><p><strong>Organisation:</strong> Annahme, Kontrolle und Verräumung von Waren sowie das Vorbereiten des Mise-en-Place für den Folgetag</p></li><li><p><strong>Teamgeist &amp; Schnittstelle:</strong> Enge Abstimmung mit dem Team zur Gewährleistung eines reibungslosen Ablaufs</p></li></ul> <br> <p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Was Du brauchst, um mit uns nach den Sternen zu greifen:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="isSelectedEnd">Ausgeprägte Kommunikationsstärke in Deutsch und Englisch sowie ein souveränes Auftreten</p></li><li><p class="isSelectedEnd">Idealerweise erste Erfahrung in Gastronomie, Hotellerie oder im Serviceumfeld</p></li><li><p class="isSelectedEnd">Organisationsfähigkeit und die Fähigkeit, auch in lebhaften Situationen strukturiert zu arbeiten</p></li><li><p class="isSelectedEnd">Flexibilität sowie Bereitschaft zu Schicht- und Wochenendarbeit</p></li><li><p>Teamgeist, Eigeninitiative und eine ausgeprägte Hands-on-Mentalität</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Darum wirst du deinen “Aufenthalt” bei uns lieben:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Onboarding und Feedback:</strong> Wir sorgen mit unserem gut durchdachten Onboarding-Prozess für einen reibungslosen Start. Regelmäßiges Feedback und Peer Reviews unterstützen dich zusätzlich in deiner Weiterentwicklung.&nbsp;</p></li><li><p><strong>OneTeam:</strong> Eine offene Unternehmenskultur mit Team-Stand-ups, regelmäßigen All-Hands-Meetings und Firmenevents (Sommerparty, Wiesn,...).</p></li><li><p><strong>Alles für unsere Limehomies:</strong> Bis zu 24 bezahlte Urlaubstage im Jahr, Rabatte bei Urban Sports Club, Unterstützung beim Thema psychische Gesundheit (Nilo.health), Staycations in einem unserer Limehomes und viele weitere Vorteile.</p></li><li><p><strong>Wettbewerbsfähiges Gehalt</strong>: Unsere faire Vergütung für Werkstudierende 15€ (Bachelor)/17€ (Master) ermöglichen dir einen komfortablen Lebensstil</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Über Limehome:</strong></p><p>Limehome ist ein führender, technologiebasierter Hospitality-Betreiber, der funktional gestaltete Designunterkünfte in ganz Europa anbietet. Durch den Einsatz seiner proprietären Technologie ermöglicht Limehome einen reibungslosen und komfortablen Aufenthalt mit einem nahtlosen digitalen Gästeerlebnis für Geschäfts- und Urlaubsreisende. Gegründet im Jahr 2018, beschäftigt Limehome heute über 300 Mitarbeitende  und zählt über 13.000 Limehome Apartments und Hotelzimmer in 150 Städten in 13 europäischen Ländern. </p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/limehome/werkstudentin-guest-service-munich-167567","tags":["Hospitality Operations"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"Munich, Bayern, Germany","created_at":1793645484},{"slug":"remote-senior-backend-engineer-go-berlin-189894","company_name":"Recare Deutschland GmbH","title":"Senior Backend Engineer (Go) (m/w/d)","description":"<p class="p1"><br></p><p class="p1"><strong>About us<br></strong></p><p class="p1">As one of Germany's leading HealthTech companies, we are transforming discharge management by making it technology driven, patient centered, and free of bureaucracy. In addition to our market leading SaaS platform, we are developing AI solutions that radically simplify processes in clinics and for aftercare providers, relieve the burden on healthcare professionals, and put the focus back on patients. We currently connect over two thirds of all German hospitals with more than 650 rehabilitation clinics, and over 25,000 care and homecare providers. With around 120 employees from a broad range of nations, we are continuing to grow and are looking for people with the right attitude who want to improve the healthcare system alongside us.</p><p class="p1" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="p1">We're now going far beyond our core business, aiming to eliminate bureaucracy and admin in hospitals with a whole portfolio of AI products.<br></p><p class="p1"><strong>What you'll work on<br></strong></p><p class="p1">Aftercare provider operations are becoming increasingly complex and data driven. Bringing change is very hard, but we're not afraid. You'll build features that help care facilities, rehabilitation centers, and healthcare chains better allocate resources, unlock actionable insights from patient data, and integrate Recare seamlessly into their internal systems.</p><p class="p1">Our ambitious roadmap focuses on expanding our marketplace's receiver side with enhanced analytics tools, B2C platforms connecting providers directly with patients, expanded API integrations, and much more.</p><p class="p1">Secure communication is at our core. Our solution provides end to end encryption for healthcare professionals to safely exchange messages and patient data through both our applications and external API integrations.<br><br><br></p><p class="p1">In this role, you will:<br></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul class="ul1"><li><p>Own a domain inside our core Go codebase, contributing to architecture decisions and code quality within your area</p></li><li><p>Work inside a well structured system with some standalone services around the edges, including an on premise gateway for hospital integrations, rather than a sprawling microservices estate</p></li><li><p>Step in and keep things moving when your lead is away, taking ownership with confidence rather than waiting for instruction</p></li><li><p>Contribute to pull requests, reviews, and technical discussions as a trusted senior voice on your team<br><br></p></li></ul><p class="p1">We have several products in development that we are confident will significantly impact the German healthcare system. And yes, we're excited by the new opportunities AI unlocks for building powerful features for our customers and our own workflow.<br><br></p><p class="p1"><strong>What technologies you'll work with<br></strong></p><ul class="ul1"><li><p><strong>Golang.</strong> Our entire backend codebase is in Golang, and we love it. It's easy to learn, it's strongly typed, the internal tooling is fantastic, and it compiles fast.</p></li><li><p><strong>Postgres.</strong> We use Postgres for our databases and GORM to interface with it.</p></li><li><p><strong>CI and DevOps.</strong> We use both CircleCI and GitHub Actions to run our unit and integration tests, visual regression tests built in house, and automated code analysis through SonarCloud. They're also used to deploy to our various environments.<br><br></p></li></ul><p class="p1">We also dedicate some of our time to work on non business tasks, which means for instance:<br><br></p><ul class="ul1"><li><p>Continuously optimising the backend code to offer the best user experience</p></li><li><p>Analysing and improving database slowdowns and issues</p></li><li><p>Internal automation, because we want to make our lives easier</p></li><li><p>Building additional tooling, such as performance profiling tools to identify bottlenecks in backend services and optimise resource usage<br><br></p></li></ul><p class="p1">Our philosophy is that developers are owners of the code they write until it gets to production. We rely a lot on automated tests to ensure everything stays stable. The rule is that code could be deployed at any time, and manual QA is only involved in new feature validation.<br><br><br></p><p class="p1"><strong>This is what you can expect from us<br><br></strong></p><ul class="ul1"><li><p><strong>Work with Purpose.</strong> Your work has a real impact on patients and healthcare professionals in the medical field.</p></li><li><p><strong>Corporate Culture.</strong> We embrace structures that foster high performance and strong team dynamics. Our interactions are characterized by mutual respect, loyalty, and recognition. We work together towards common goals and expect the same from you.</p></li><li><p><strong>Flexibility.</strong> Would you like to pick up your child from daycare? Do you enjoy exercising during lunchtime? We support you in achieving that balance. Besides flexible working hours, as a remote-first company we offer the flexibility to work 100% remotely from Germany, Spain, Portugal, Italy, Poland, France and Austria.</p></li><li><p><strong>Edenred card,</strong> which you can use in the way that suits you best.</p></li><li><p><strong>Extra Day Off on Your Birthday,</strong> so you can celebrate with your loved ones.<br><br><br></p></li></ul><p class="p1"><strong>Your responsibilities as a Senior Backend Engineer will include<br></strong></p><ul class="ul1"><li><p><strong>Technical Ownership.</strong> Own a domain inside our Go codebase, contribute to architectural decisions and code quality within your area, identify bottlenecks and inefficiencies and suggest or implement improvements.</p></li><li><p><strong>Stepping Up When Needed.</strong> Be ready to take charge of priorities and keep things moving if your lead is away, supporting and mentoring other engineers along the way without needing to manage a team.</p></li><li><p><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration.</strong> Work closely with product and design to translate business needs into technical solutions, and communicate technical progress, risks and trade-offs clearly.</p></li><li><p><strong>Delivery.</strong> Ship reliably against the team's roadmap, help break down features into deliverable tasks, and identify and remove blockers as they come up.</p></li><li><p><strong>Building With AI.</strong> We are an AI company now, and that shows up in how we expect people to work, not just what we build. Use AI tooling as a genuine part of your day to day, whether that is accelerating how you write and review code, prototyping ideas faster, or finding smarter ways to work. We do not expect you to vibe code everything end to end, plenty of our best engineers still want to write the core of what they ship themselves and use AI to speed things up around the edges. What matters is real curiosity about where this is heading, not scepticism about whether any of this changes how software gets built.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p class="p1"><br>What you will need to succeed as a Senior Backend Engineer:<br></p><ul class="ul1"><li><p>We are looking for experienced developers. You have a CS degree or equivalent knowledge, and you have been coding full time professionally for 4 to 5 plus years</p></li><li><p>We're looking for someone with production experience in Golang, or another C family language with a real, demonstrable ability to operate in Go without hand holding</p></li><li><p>You have some experience supporting or mentoring other engineers, and you are looking for a strong individual contributor role rather than a path into people management</p></li><li><p>You want to become a technical owner of part of our codebase. We need people who are looking for responsibility, just not a team to manage</p></li><li><p>You are a clear, confident communicator, comfortable being put on the spot in a conversation and able to think out loud rather than defaulting to async only communication when something needs a real time answer</p></li><li><p>Since Product and Engineering work in a fully remote setup, writing skills matter more and more, so written questions, requirements, and docs are genuinely valuable</p></li><li><p>You should be comfortable and excited to dive into more advanced topics, for example build pipelines, caching mechanisms, and database optimisation</p></li><li><p>Since we're a small team, we want to automate a lot. You should have experience with CI and testing frameworks</p></li><li><p>You are proactive and proficient across the entire product development flow, asking questions, clarifying specs, raising doubts, and engaging in meetings</p></li><li><p>Healthcare experience is a bonus, not a requirement. FHIR, HL7, or DICOM exposure is great to have, but we have hired strong engineers from fintech, insurtech, and other compliance heavy domains with zero healthcare background who did just fine</p></li><li><p>You are genuinely excited about what AI can do for engineering. We don't expect every line of code to be AI generated, but we do expect curiosity and a real point of view on where this is heading</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 class="text-text-100 mt-3 -mb-1 text-[1.125rem] font-bold"></h3><h4 class="text-text-100 mt-2 -mb-1 text-base font-bold"></h4><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/recare-deutschland-gmbh/remote-senior-backend-engineer-go-berlin-189894","tags":["Engineering","Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1793645484},{"slug":"remote-senior-data-engineer-berlin-467823","company_name":"Recare Deutschland GmbH","title":"Senior Data Engineer (m/f/d)","description":"<p>As one of the leading German HealthTech companies, we are reshaping discharge management – technology-driven, patient-centered, and free from bureaucracy. In addition to our market-leading SaaS platform, we develop AI solutions that radically simplify processes in hospitals and for aftercare providers, relieve healthcare professionals, and refocus attention on patients. Today, we already connect two-thirds of all German hospitals with over 650 rehabilitation clinics and 25,000 nursing and homecare providers. With currently around 100 employees, we continue to grow – and we are looking for people with character who want to help us improve the healthcare system and solve administrative complexity across care journeys in Europe.<br></p><p>Our data flows from our applications, product events and business systems, in a highly regulated healthcare context. This role exists to build the platform that makes sure that data arrives complete, on time and safe to use, so Product, leadership, RevOps and Finance work from the same numbers.<br></p><p>You will be the first data engineer in a new data team that sits in Product, works across the company and reports to the Head of Data. You will own the platform that moves our data into Snowflake and shape the architecture decisions around it: which tools we build on, how pipelines are orchestrated and monitored, and how data infrastructure is managed as code.<br><br></p><h2><span style="font-size:0.9em">What to expect</span></h2><p>This is what you can expect from us as a Senior Data Engineer:</p><ul><li><p>Purposeful work – your work gives the teams serving hospitals and aftercare providers data they can trust.</p></li><li><p>Real ownership – as the first data engineer in a new team, you shape the data platform and its tooling.</p></li><li><p>Company culture – we believe in flat hierarchies that promote high performance and strong team dynamics. We foster an environment characterized by mutual respect, loyalty, and recognition. Together, we strive for our goals – and expect the same from you.</p></li><li><p>Flexibility – want to pick up your child from daycare? Like to exercise during lunch? We'll support you. We are a remote-friendly company offering flexible working hours. Workations are also possible by arrangement.</p></li><li><p>Edenred card – which you can use according to your needs.</p></li></ul><p>Extra vacation day – so you can celebrate your birthday with your loved ones, you'll have the day off.<br></p><h2><span style="font-size:0.9em">This is how you will make an impact as a Senior Data Engineer:</span></h2><ul><li><p>Data from our application databases, product events and SaaS tools needs to reach Snowflake reliably. You build and run that ingestion and decide where to buy a managed connector and where to build.</p></li><li><p>Our pipelines need clear dependencies, retries, alerting and SLAs. You set up orchestration so a failed or partial load stops downstream work instead of silently producing wrong numbers.</p></li><li><p>New products need event pipelines. You design them together with engineers, keeping patient data out of analytics events by design.</p></li><li><p>Product and Finance need to work from the same definitions. You maintain the dbt models that connect product usage with customer, billing and revenue data.</p></li><li><p>Our CRM (HubSpot) and our internal systems need to talk to each other. You build the data flows between them, including two-way synchronisation where it is needed.</p></li><li><p>Data quality problems need to be caught before a dashboard or a board report does. You establish validation, monitoring and alerting.</p></li><li><p>Our data needs strong privacy and access controls. You enforce role-based access and masking in Snowflake, pseudonymisation, and deletion that propagates across raw and modelled data.</p></li><li><p>Data code needs the same engineering standards as our product code. You bring code review, testing, documentation and CI/CD to it.</p></li></ul><h2><span style="font-size:0.9em">How we build</span></h2><p>We run a modern cloud-native stack to move, model and protect data reliably in a regulated healthcare environment.</p><ul><li><p>Cloud: AWS (The European Sovereign Cloud partition)</p></li><li><p>Runtime: Kubernetes (EKS) and Postgres (RDS)</p></li><li><p>Warehouse and modelling: Snowflake (EU), dbt</p></li><li><p>Orchestration: Airflow or Dagster (being introduced)</p></li><li><p>BI: Looker</p></li><li><p>Observability: Datadog</p></li><li><p>CI/CD: GitHub Enterprise Cloud with Actions</p></li><li><p>Infrastructure: CloudFormation</p></li><li><p>Business systems: HubSpot, Chargebee</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <ul><li><p>Several years (typically 5 or more) building production data pipelines, as a data engineer or as a backend engineer on data-intensive systems.</p></li><li><p>Strong Python: you write tested, maintainable production code, not only scripts.</p></li><li><p>Advanced SQL, including window functions, CTEs and query optimisation.</p></li><li><p>Production experience with Snowflake or a comparable cloud warehouse: compute sizing and cost control, role-based access, masking, and performance tuning.</p></li><li><p>Experience with dbt, or a similar tool for tested and documented transformations.</p></li><li><p>Solid ingestion fundamentals: initial versus incremental loads, change data capture from Postgres, idempotency, schema evolution, late and out-of-order data, and backfills.</p></li><li><p>Production experience with an orchestrator such as Airflow or Dagster.</p></li><li><p>Experience with AWS and with deploying your own work in containers.</p></li><li><p>A data quality mindset: you profile data, test assumptions and build checks.</p></li><li><p>Practical knowledge of GDPR: you can identify personal data and implement pseudonymisation, access control and deletion.</p></li><li><p>You use AI coding tools in your daily work and know where they help and where they need checking.</p></li><li><p>Ability to own decisions as the only data engineer and to explain technical trade-offs to non-engineers.</p></li><li><p>Preference for writing over talking, resulting in clear, concise, yet complete documentation and asynchronous communications.</p></li><li><p>Fluent English, written and spoken. Other languages are a plus.<br></p></li></ul><h3>Bonus points</h3><ul><li><p>Healthcare or regulated-domain experience (e.g. ISO 27001, C5).</p></li><li><p>Integrating CRM and SaaS systems such as HubSpot or Salesforce, including reverse ETL or two-way sync.</p></li><li><p>Designing product event tracking (e.g. Snowplow or Segment).</p></li><li><p>Kubernetes in production.</p></li><li><p>Reading and changing Go code.</p></li><li><p>Managing Snowflake as code.</p></li><li><p>German language skills.<br></p></li></ul><h3>Our values</h3><p>This will help you decide if you want to join us – our values are:</p><ul><li><p>Strong opinions, weakly held. We adapt, negotiate trade-offs, and reconsider decisions when necessary. We don't stick to one implementation – we re-evaluate and adjust as needed (including throwing away the old one).</p></li><li><p>Pragmatic choice of tools and avoidance of one-size-fits-all thinking.</p></li><li><p>Bringing professionalism and empathy to how you work with others.</p></li><li><p>Strong belief in solid technical fundamentals and preference for understanding and first principles over memorization.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/recare-deutschland-gmbh/remote-senior-data-engineer-berlin-467823","tags":["Product","Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1793645484},{"slug":"fachinformatiker-systemintegration-zell-326813","company_name":"Lamm HR GmbH","title":"Fachinformatiker Systemintegration (m/w/d)","description":"<p class="MsoNormal">Für unseren Kunden, eine der führenden Weinkellereien Deutschlands suchen wir zum nächstmöglichen Zeitpunkt am Standort Zell einen qualifizierten <strong>Fachinformatiker Systemintegration (m/w/d).</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Deine Aufgaben:</strong></p><ul><li><p class="MsoNormal">Installation, Administration, Implementierung und Weiterentwicklung der gesamten IT-Infrastruktur</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Sicherstellung von Netzwerk- und Datensicherheit</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Gewährleistung und Umsetzung von IT-Security-Themen</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Überwachung und Optimierung von Netzwerk und Systemen</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Installation, Einrichtung und Aufbau von Clientsystemen</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Planung, Aufbau und Wartung von (Windows-) Serversystemen (in VMWare-Infrastruktur)</p></li><li><p class="MsoNormal">Lösung und Dokumentation von Anwendungs- und Systemproblemen (