s and our Slough HQ. We’re proud of our close-knit culture, where we speak up, celebrate differences and push boundaries together.</p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>About the role</strong></p><p>This is an exciting opportunity to join a site that is investing in its future. As our Area Engineering Manager, you'll play a key role in supporting significant growth initiatives, helping to embed new production capability and maximise the performance of world-class manufacturing equipment.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>You'll lead a team of Maintenance Leads and Engineers, creating a culture of accountability, development and continuous improvement. Working closely with operational and strategic stakeholders, you'll drive engineering performance, equipment reliability and operational excellence across your area.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>This role is ideal for someone who combines strong technical expertise with a growth mindset. You'll have the opportunity to influence change, contribute to major improvement projects and help shape the future of engineering at the site. If you're motivated by developing people, delivering results and leaving things better than you found them, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What’s in it for you?</strong><br>We believe in rewarding our colleagues and helping them thrive. Here’s a flavour of what we offer:</p><ul><li><p>Competitive annual salary, annual salary review and annual bonus opportunity (target 7.5%), plus a £6,000 car allowance. </p></li><li><p>KP Pension Plan with up to 7% matched contributions</p></li><li><p>25 days holiday, with the option to buy up to five additional days, plus additional holiday after five years’ service</p></li><li><p>Comprehensive healthcare including Single Cover Private Healthcare, Health Cash Plan, Digital GP and Employee Assistance Programme</p></li><li><p>Electric Vehicle Car Scheme, supporting more sustainable and cost-effective travel</p></li><li><p>KP4ME benefits platform with discounts, cashback and wellbeing support</p></li><li><p>Enhanced family-friendly policies to support colleagues at every stage of life</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What will you be doing?</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Leading and developing engineering teams </strong>- Coach, support and develop Maintenance Leads and Engineering colleagues, building capability and creating a high-performing culture</p></li><li><p><strong>Driving reliability and performance </strong>- Ensure equipment operates safely and efficiently through effective preventative maintenance planning, resource management and continuous improvement activity</p></li><li><p><strong>Supporting site growth and investment projects</strong> - Play a key role in the implementation and optimisation of new production lines and equipment, helping deliver strategic growth objectives</p></li><li><p><strong>Improving engineering standards and processes </strong>- Drive improvements in Overall Equipment Effectiveness (OEE), downtime reduction, maintenance strategies and asset performance</p></li><li><p><strong>Collaborating across the site leadership team </strong> - Work closely with operational and strategic stakeholders to deliver projects, manage priorities and support the site's long-term engineering vision</p></li></ul> <br> <p style="text-align:start;"><strong>We’d love to hear from you if you can bring:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Engineering qualifications and technical expertise </strong>- Qualified in Mechanical and/or Electrical Engineering (HNC/HND, Degree, or equivalent). &nbsp;FMCG manufacturing experience, and knowledge of CMMS, TPM, and RCA methodologies desirable.</p></li><li><p><strong>People leadership experience </strong>- Previous experience leading, coaching and developing engineering teams, with a genuine passion for helping others succeed</p></li><li><p><strong>A continuous improvement mindset </strong>- Experience identifying opportunities to improve reliability, efficiency, performance and ways of working</p></li><li><p><strong>Strong planning and organisational skills </strong>- Able to balance reactive priorities while delivering preventative maintenance programmes and longer-term objectives</p></li><li><p><strong>Excellent stakeholder management skills </strong>- Confident working with colleagues at all levels to influence decisions, solve problems and deliver results</p></li><li><p><strong>Project or budget management experience </strong>- Exposure to capital projects, site investment programmes or budget management would be advantageous, but is not essential</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Our purpose</strong><br>At KP Snacks, we're passionate about <em>creating happy snacking moments</em> through our great tasting snacks and iconic brands. Every day, millions of people enjoy our products, including Hula Hoops, McCoy's, KP Nuts, Tyrrells, Skips, POM-BEAR and Butterkist, making us one of the UK's leading snack manufacturers.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">For decades, we've been delighting consumers by combining well-loved favourites with exciting innovations that reflect changing tastes and expectations. We're equally passionate about our people and committed to creating a workplace where everyone can grow, develop and make a real impact.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="MsoNormal">As part of the Intersnack Group, one of the world's leading snack manufacturers, we combine global expertise with a shared commitment to <em>creating happy snacking moments</em> every day.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>We’re committed to inclusion</strong><br>We’re building a workplace where everyone belongs. If you don’t tick every box, we’d still love to hear from you – your unique perspective could be just what we need. And if there’s anything we can do to make the process easier for you, just let us know.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>#LI-Onsite </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/kp-snacks/area-engineering-manager-ashby-de-la-zouch-338565","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Ashby de la Zouch, England, United Kingdom","created_at":1793709100},{"slug":"customer-service-and-sales-administaror-sidcup-99425","company_name":"Cloverleaf Plumbing Heating & Renewables Ltd","title":"Customer Service and Sales administaror","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p>Cloverleaf Plumbing, Heating & Renewables is a well-established and growing business, proudly serving customers since 1994.</p><p>We specialise in plumbing, heating, air conditioning and renewable energy solutions, helping homeowners and businesses improve their comfort and energy efficiency.</p><p>As our business continues to grow, we're looking for an enthusiastic, organised and confident individual to join our friendly office team.</p><h2>About the Role</h2><p>This is an exciting opportunity for someone who enjoys working with people, thrives in a busy office environment, and wants to develop their career in customer relationship and sales.</p><p><strong>Initially, the role will focus primarily on general office administration, customer service and supporting the smooth day-to-day running of the business.</strong></p><p>However, we're looking for more than someone who simply processes paperwork.</p><p>You'll also play an important role in how we welcome new customers, manage incoming enquiries and guide prospective clients through the early stages of their journey with Cloverleaf.</p><p>As you become familiar with our services, systems and customers, there will be opportunities to take on greater sales responsibilities, develop your commercial skills and earn additional income through a commission structure.</p><p>You don't need to be a heating or renewable energy expert. We're much more interested in finding someone with the right personality, communication skills and willingness to learn.</p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><h3>Office Administration & Operations</h3><ul><li><p>Manage and coordinate boiler and air source heat pump servicing, including customer reminders, bookings and follow-up communications.</p></li><li><p>Complete manufacturer product and warranty registrations, ensuring accurate records are maintained.</p></li><li><p>Assist with the administration of our company vehicle fleet, including servicing, MOTs, insurance and general vehicle records.</p></li><li><p>Maintain accurate customer information, job records and documentation within our Simpro management system.</p></li><li><p>Support the scheduling and coordination of engineers and customer appointments.</p></li><li><p>Liaise with customers, engineers, suppliers and other members of the team to ensure jobs progress smoothly.</p></li><li><p>Assist with general office administration and other operational tasks as required.</p></li></ul><h3>Customer Enquiries & Relationship Management</h3><ul><li><p>Act as a friendly, professional and confident first point of contact for customers contacting Cloverleaf by telephone, email or through our website.</p></li><li><p>Handle new sales enquiries, asking relevant questions to understand customers' requirements and identify the most appropriate next step.</p></li><li><p>Qualify and organise incoming enquiries, ensuring customers are directed towards the correct service, appointment or member of the team.</p></li><li><p>Build rapport with prospective customers and maintain communication throughout the early stages of their enquiry.</p></li><li><p>Arrange initial consultations, surveys and follow-up appointments with the appropriate team members.</p></li><li><p>Proactively follow up with prospective customers, keeping conversations moving forward and ensuring opportunities are not overlooked.</p></li><li><p>Maintain accurate customer notes and enquiry records to support a structured and professional sales process.</p></li></ul><h3>Sales Development & Career Progression</h3><p>As you gain experience and confidence, we would like you to become increasingly involved in the commercial side of the business.</p><p>This could include:</p><ul><li><p>Following up on quotations and helping customers make informed purchasing decisions.</p></li><li><p>Developing the confidence to discuss our services, explain their benefits and address common customer objections.</p></li><li><p>Managing your own customer enquiries and progressing opportunities through the sales process.</p></li><li><p>Helping convert enquiries into confirmed appointments and accepted quotations.</p></li><li><p>Working towards agreed sales targets with the opportunity to earn commission.</p></li></ul><p>Full training and ongoing support will be provided as your responsibilities develop.</p><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><p>We're looking for someone who combines excellent organisational skills with a natural ability to communicate and build relationships.</p><h3>Essential Skills & Qualities</h3><ul><li><p>Previous experience in office administration, customer service or a similar role.</p></li><li><p>Confident, friendly and professional telephone manner.</p></li><li><p>Comfortable starting conversations with new customers and asking questions to understand their needs.</p></li><li><p>Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage several tasks and priorities.</p></li><li><p>Excellent attention to detail and a reliable approach to completing administrative work.</p></li><li><p>Good written communication and computer skills.</p></li><li><p>A proactive attitude, with the confidence to take ownership of tasks and follow them through.</p></li><li><p>Willingness to learn new systems, processes and technical information.</p></li><li><p>A positive, enthusiastic personality and the ability to work well within a small team.</p></li><li><p>An interest in developing customer relationship and sales skills.</p></li></ul><h3>Desirable Experience</h3><ul><li><p>Experience working in plumbing, heating, air conditioning, renewables, construction or a related industry.</p></li><li><p>Previous experience in a customer-facing sales or sales support role.</p></li><li><p>Experience using CRM or job management software such as Simpro.</p></li><li><p>Experience managing service schedules, customer appointments or maintenance contracts.</p></li><li><p>Previous involvement in following up on quotations or converting customer enquiries into sales.</p></li></ul><p>Industry experience is an advantage but is not essential. We believe that the right attitude, personality and communication skills are just as important as previous technical knowledge.</p><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul><li><p>Competitive basic salary of £26,000–£29,000 per annum, depending on experience.</p></li><li><p><strong>Opportunity to earn additional sales commission as your role develops.</strong></p></li><li><p>20 days' annual leave plus 8 bank holidays.</p></li><li><p>An additional 3 days' paid holiday gifted by the company during our Christmas shutdown.</p></li><li><p>Workplace pension scheme.</p></li><li><p>Friendly, supportive and established team environment.</p></li><li><p>Training on our products, services and business systems.</p></li><li><p>Genuine opportunities for professional development as the company continues to grow.</p></li><li><p>The opportunity to play an important role in a growing business within the renewable energy sector.</p></li></ul><h2>How to Apply</h2><p>If you're organised, enjoy speaking with people and would like a role that offers both variety and the opportunity to develop your career, we'd love to hear from you.</p><p>We're particularly interested in hearing from candidates who are confident on the telephone, enjoy building customer relationships and are motivated to take on more responsibility over time.</p><p>Please apply with your up-to-date CV and a brief introduction explaining why you feel you'd be a good fit for our team.</p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/cloverleaf-plumbing-heating-renewables-ltd/customer-service-and-sales-administaror-sidcup-99425","tags":["Customer Service"],"job_types":["Permanent employment contract (open-ended contract)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Sidcup","created_at":1793709070},{"slug":"mobile-paid-user-acquisition-manager-london-354673","company_name":"REPLUG","title":"Mobile Paid User Acquisition Manager (m/f/d)","description":"<p>Are you fascinated by performance marketing and can't wait to open your laptop in the morning to see how your latest ad campaign is performing? Do you eat Lookalikes for breakfast and drink coffee with CPAs? <strong>Then keep reading!</strong></p><h2><strong>About REPLUG</strong></h2><p>REPLUG is a Mobile Revenue Growth partner that helps companies turn mobile into a measurable driver of revenue, customer value, and long-term business growth.</p><p>From global app publishers to established brands looking to unlock more value from mobile, we partner with companies that want to grow more efficiently, reduce dependency on saturated acquisition channels, and build sustainable growth.</p><p>Our work combines strategic thinking with hands-on execution across App Store Optimization, Paid User Acquisition, CRM, measurement, and mobile growth consulting.</p><p>REPLUG is looking for an experienced <strong>Mobile Paid User Acquisition Manager (m/f/d)</strong>, eager to take the next steps in their mobile marketing career working in a fast-growing international agency.</p><p>You will have the opportunity to deepen your knowledge of mobile paid user acquisition, working alongside top industry specialists, launching, scaling, and optimizing mobile performance campaigns for our clients' portfolio, from subscription apps to mobile games.</p><h2><strong>Your responsibilities</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Setting up and managing <strong>performance advertising campaigns on major Paid Social Media platforms</strong> (Facebook, Instagram, Twitter, Snapchat, TikTok, etc.).</p></li><li><p>Setting up and managing campaigns on Google Ads and Apple Search Ads</p></li><li><p>Managing and analyzing campaigns on main Mobile DSPs (Applovin, Moloco, Mintegral, Kayzen, Unity, etc).</p></li><li><p>Taking care of <strong>MMP (Mobile Measurement Partners) setup</strong> to ensure proper monitoring by our Mobile Paid User Acquisition team</p></li><li><p>Creation and updating of <strong>performance reports</strong> based on targeted KPIs on tools such as Google Sheet, Google Data Studio, Tableau, etc.</p></li><li><p>Continuous analysis and optimization of user acquisition and retargeting campaigns to achieve our clients' business goals.</p></li><li><p>Prepare <strong>creative briefs</strong> for our graphics team so that we always have new creative for campaigns.</p></li><li><p>Use UGC (user-generated content) tools to find the best creators to promote our clients' apps.</p></li><li><p>Exploring <strong>artificial intelligence tools</strong> to improve our creative production process and our advertising activities in general</p></li><li><p>Answer our clients' questions on campaigns, performance and setup independently, and explain why the numbers look the way they do.</p></li><li><p>Take responsibility for your accounts' targets and KPIs, flag early when we're at risk of missing them, and come with concrete proposals for what to do about it.</p></li><li><p>Consult with our clients on tracking & analytics topics such as SKAN, MMP, Attribution, etc.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Requirements</strong></h2><ul><li><p>You have <strong>3+ years</strong> of proven success in managing paid user acquisition channels for mobile applications</p></li><li><p>You have in-depth knowledge of the main Mobile Measurement Partners tools (Adjust, Appsflyer, Branch, Kochava, etc.) and know all about tracking and attribution</p></li><li><p>You know how to set up <strong>Apple's SKAd network</strong></p></li><li><p>You are familiar with Excel, Google Data Studio, Tableau or other BI tools</p></li><li><p>You understand the importance of reporting, both to improve results and to show the client how good you are.</p></li><li><p>You have good presentation skills and can use Google Slides, Keynote and Power Point</p></li><li><p>You believe that <strong>small details can make a big difference</strong></p></li><li><p>You like to question every accomplishment to figure out how to improve.</p></li><li><p>You keep track of your own open items, hit the deadlines you commit to, and raise it early when something is at risk, instead of waiting to be asked.</p></li><li><p>You are proactive and bring an entrepreneurial mindset to the team</p></li><li><p>You're a firm believer in <strong>sharing knowledge</strong> and eager to contribute to the community through content creation and speaking engagements</p></li><li><p>You are fluent in English, but other languages are welcome.</p></li><li><p>Plus: Basic understanding of app store optimization strategies.</p></li><li><p>Plus: Use of tools such as Claude, Canva, Midjourney, CapCut is highly valued.</p></li></ul><p><strong>We know it's a lot of requirements, but we value transparency and like to be clear up front about what we expect from you :-)</strong></p><h2><strong>Working conditions and perks</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Home Office support for your remote setup.</p></li><li><p>Mentoring sessions to support your professional development.</p></li><li><p>Remote work flexibility based across the European Union.</p></li><li><p>Vouchers and discounts.</p></li><li><p>24 vacation days per year.</p></li><li><p>Competitive base + performance-driven commission</p></li><li><p>High autonomy, zero bureaucracy</p></li><li><p>Direct access to founders and decision-makers</p></li><li><p>Education budget (courses, conferences, certifications)</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/replug/mobile-paid-user-acquisition-manager-london-354673","tags":["Remote","Online Marketing"],"job_types":["Fixed-term contract","contract","manager"],"location":"London","created_at":1793701885},{"slug":"senior-counsel-privacy-ai-compliance-eu-london-germany-spain-292202","company_name":"Coreweaveu","title":"Senior Counsel, Privacy & AI Compliance (EU)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;gmail_quote&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;m_-113912706363268805m_-2746164444908759431gmail-docs-internal-guid-131e4fb0-7fff-b4e9-ff50-e8cf32449b1b&quot;&gt;CoreWeave is The Essential Cloud for AI™. Built for pioneers by pioneers, CoreWeave delivers a platform of technology, tools, and teams that enables innovators to build and scale AI with confidence. Trusted by leading AI labs, startups, and global enterprises, CoreWeave combines superior infrastructure performance with deep technical expertise to accelerate breakthroughs and turn compute into capability. Founded in 2017, CoreWeave became a publicly traded company (Nasdaq: CRWV) in March 2025. Learn more at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coreweave.com&quot;&gt;www.coreweave.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We&#39;re proud to be a Living Wage accredited Employer.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Legal and Government Affairs team at CoreWeave is highly collaborative and partners closely with teams across the company to navigate complex legal landscapes while enabling innovation and growth. The team is pragmatic, solutions-oriented, and deeply engaged in strategic decision-making, with a strong emphasis on building trusted relationships across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Senior Counsel, Privacy &amp;amp; AI Compliance (EU)&lt;/strong&gt;, you will serve as a key legal advisor on European privacy, data protection, and artificial intelligence requirements. If you thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced environment, enjoy solving complex problems, and are eager to make a significant impact, CoreWeave is the place for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Senior Director &amp;amp; Lead Managing Counsel, Privacy, Regulatory &amp;amp; Compliance, you will independently advise on complex regional matters, help operationalize evolving legal requirements, and partner closely with Privacy, Product, Engineering, Security, Commercial Legal, Government Affairs, and business teams across Europe. You will play a central role in scaling practical, risk-based privacy and AI compliance frameworks for CoreWeave’s cloud infrastructure, products, and European operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this Role You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on EU and UK privacy, data protection, and AI laws and regulatory developments, including the GDPR, UK GDPR, ePrivacy requirements, the EU AI Act, the EU Data Act, and related national implementing laws and guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex legal requirements into clear, practical, and scalable guidance for Product, Engineering, Security, Commercial, Marketing, HR, Procurement, and operational teams across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or support privacy and AI assessments for new and evolving products, features, data uses, vendors, and business initiatives, including DPIAs, legitimate-interest assessments, transfer impact assessments, AI risk and classification analyses, and documented compliance decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering to embed privacy by design and default, responsible AI, data minimization, transparency, security, retention, and governance requirements into product architecture and development processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;•&amp;nbsp; Advise on international data transfers, data localization and residency requirements, cross-border access, and related contractual and operational mechanisms, including EU Standard Contractual Clauses and the UK International Data Transfer Addendum or Agreement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support implementation of CoreWeave’s AI compliance framework in Europe, including role and use-case classification, risk management, transparency, recordkeeping, human oversight, technical documentation, contractual allocation of responsibilities, and governance for internal and customer-facing AI uses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regional guidance on data subject rights, records of processing, privacy notices, consent and cookies, retention and deletion, data sharing, direct marketing, and other core privacy program requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on European product launches, market entry, strategic partnerships, customer and vendor arrangements, and commercial terms involving privacy, data use, AI, and regulatory responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cybersecurity and privacy incident response in Europe, including assessment of regulator and data subject notification obligations, engagement with relevant stakeholders, and documentation of defensible legal decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or support responses to inquiries, audits, consultations, and investigations involving European data protection authorities, AI regulators, and other governmental bodies; coordinate with local counsel and drive follow-up and remediation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain regional policies, procedures, playbooks, training, control mappings, and evidence of compliance, and monitor emerging legal and enforcement trends to inform business strategy and program priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of relevant legal experience, including substantial experience advising on European privacy and data protection matters; a mix of law firm, regulatory, and in-house experience is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified to practice law in an EU member state or the United Kingdom and in good standing with the applicable professional body.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of the GDPR and UK GDPR, including controller and processor obligations, privacy-by-design requirements, data subject rights, international transfers, DPIAs, security and breach notification, and regulator engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful experience with AI governance or emerging AI regulation, including the ability to interpret and operationalize the EU AI Act for technology, cloud, infrastructure, or enterprise use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently manage complex regional matters, identify material risk, present practical options, and make clear, defensible recommendations in ambiguous situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operationalizing privacy and AI compliance programs through policies, assessments, controls, training, governance processes, monitoring, and audit-ready documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency and the ability to understand data flows, cloud architecture, product functionality, AI systems, and security practices and translate them into actionable legal guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent drafting and communication skills, with the ability to explain complex legal requirements clearly and influence technical, commercial, and business stakeholders across jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build trusted cross-functional relationships, manage multiple priorities, and work effectively in a fast-paced, rapidly scaling global environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising a high-growth cloud, AI, SaaS, data center, infrastructure, or other technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with European data protection authorities, AI regulators, standards bodies, industry groups, or external counsel on novel technology issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on cross-border data transfers, cloud service provider obligations, enterprise AI governance, and the allocation of regulatory responsibilities between providers and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with recognized privacy, security, and AI governance frameworks or standards, such as ISO/IEC 27701, ISO/IEC 42001.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wondering if you’re a good fit? We believe in investing in our people, and value candidates who can bring their own diversified experiences to our teams – even if you aren&#39;t a 100% skill or experience match. Here are a few qualities we’ve found compatible with our team. If some of this describes you, we’d love to talk.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You remain calm under pressure and can make sound, defensible decisions when facts are still developing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re curious about technology and enjoy working closely with security and engineering teams to understand how systems operate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate complex legal risk clearly and concisely, with a practical focus on protecting customers and enabling the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why CoreWeave?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoreWeave, we work hard, have fun, and move fast!&amp;nbsp; We’re in an exciting stage of hyper-growth that you will not want to miss out on. We’re not afraid of a little chaos, and we’re constantly learning. Our team cares deeply about how we build our product and how we work together, which is represented through our core values:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Curious at Your Core&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act Like an Owner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower Employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver Best-in-Class Client Experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve More Together&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support and encourage an entrepreneurial outlook and independent thinking. We foster an environment that encourages collaboration and enables the development of innovative solutions to complex problems. As we get set for takeoff, the organization&#39;s growth opportunities are constantly expanding. You will be surrounded by some of the best talent in the industry, who will want to learn from you, too. Come join us!&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting salary will be determined by job-related knowledge, skills, experience, and the market location. We strive for both market alignment and internal equity when determining compensation. In addition to base salary, our total rewards package includes a discretionary bonus, equity awards, and a comprehensive benefits program (all based on eligibility).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;To fulfill our obligation to protect client data, successful applicants offered employment with CoreWeave will be required to complete a basic criminal record check, conducted in compliance with GDPR. Employment offers are conditional upon receiving satisfactory check results.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, we offer a variety of benefits to support your needs, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Medical Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Family-level Dental Insurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous Pension Contribution&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance at 4x Salary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Critical Illness Cover&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Assistance Programme&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work culture focused on innovative disruption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Benefits may vary by location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CoreWeave is an equal opportunity employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and supportive workplace. All qualified applicants and candidates will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Agencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;CoreWeave does not accept speculative CVs. Any unsolicited CVs received will be treated as the property of CoreWeave and your Terms &amp;amp; Conditions associated with the use of CVs will be considered null and void.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-stringify-type=&quot;italic&quot;&gt;Any unsolicited CVs sent by your company to us – that is to say, in any situation where we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy – will be considered by us to be a “free gift”, leaving us liable for no fees whatsoever should we choose to contact the candidate directly and engage the candidate’s services, and will in no way establish any prior claim by your company to representation of that candidate should the candidate’s details also be submitted by any other party.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Export Control Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires access to export controlled information. &amp;nbsp;To conform to U.S. Government export regulations applicable to that information, applicant must either be (A) a U.S. person, defined as a (i) U.S. citizen or national, (ii) U.S. lawful permanent resident (green card holder), (iii) refugee under 8 U.S.C. § 1157, or (iv) asylee under 8 U.S.C. § 1158, (B) eligible to access the export controlled information without a required export authorization, or (C) eligible and reasonably likely to obtain the required export authorization from the applicable U.S. government agency. &amp;nbsp;CoreWeave may, for legitimate business reasons, decline to pursue any export licensing process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Updated privacy notice - UK and EU Job Applications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;When you apply to a job on this site, the personal data contained in your application will be collected by CoreWeave UK Ltd. (“Controller”), which is located at&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Phosphor (6th Floor), 133 Park Street, London, SE1 9EA&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;and can be contacted by emailing ----- Controller’s data protection officer can be contacted at ----- Your personal data will be processed for the purposes of managing Controller’s recruitment related activities, which include setting up and conducting interviews and tests for applicants, evaluating and assessing the results thereto, and as is otherwise needed in the recruitment and hiring processes. Such processing is legally permissible under Art. 6(1)(f) of (i) Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”) and (ii) the GDPR as it forms part of the laws of the UK (“UK GDPR”), as necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller, which are the solicitation, evaluation, and selection of applicants for employment. Your personal data will be shared with Greenhouse Software, Inc., a cloud services provider located in the United States of America and engaged by Controller to help manage its recruitment and hiring process on Controller’s behalf. With respect to transfers originating from the UK or the European Economic Area (&quot;EEA&quot;) to a country outside the UK or the EEA, we implement the appropriate transfer mechanism(s) and other appropriate solutions to address cross-border transfers as required by applicable law. You may request a copy of the suitable mechanisms we have in place by contacting us at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a ----------
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Controller as long as Controller determines it is necessary to evaluate your application for employment. Where permitted by applicable law, we may also retain your personal data for a limited period after the recruitment process ends in order to consider you for future job opportunities, respond to legal claims, or comply with record-keeping obligations. Under the GDPR and the UK GDPR, you have the right to request access to your personal data, to request that your personal data be rectified or erased, and to request that processing of your personal data be restricted. You also have the right to data portability. In addition, you may lodge a complaint with the relevant supervisory authority: (i) A list of Europe’s data protection authorities can be found &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ec.europa.eu/justice/article-29/structure/data-protection-authorities/index_en.htm__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9xVQGfFw$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;; and (ii) for the UK, this is the &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://urldefense.com/v3/__https://ico.org.uk/__;!!I6uDfDBXfA!zaqvpaXitCAqve4cpmPGknjMlTsgIw8w_6xTVeiRpNP5Eo6Ajz9ZkXAYM2uL-nlD8kD6Ndd-Oe-k_BEQQh9IDhJOUA$&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Information Commissioner&#39;s Office&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For additional information, please see our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.coreweave.com/docs/policies/terms-of-service/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/coreweaveu/senior-counsel-privacy-ai-compliance-eu-london-germany-spain-292202","tags":["Legal & Government Affairs"],"job_types":[],"location":"London, Germany, Spain","created_at":1793699718},{"slug":"regional-field-cto-emea-germany-netherlands-france-italy-ireland-finland-sweden-37072","company_name":"Blackduck","title":"Regional Field CTO","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Black Duck Software, Inc. helps organizations build secure, high-quality software, minimizing risks while maximizing speed and productivity. Black Duck, a recognized pioneer in application security, provides SAST, SCA, and DAST solutions that enable teams to quickly find and fix vulnerabilities and defects in proprietary code, open source components, and application behavior. With a combination of industry-leading tools, services, and expertise, only Black Duck helps organizations maximize security and quality in DevSecOps and throughout the software development life cycle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional Field Chief Technology Officer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: EMEA, Remote (Black Duck has entities in UK, Germany, Netherlands, France, Italy, Ireland, Finland, Sweden)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Black Duck® meets the board-level risks of modern software with True Scale Application Security, ensuring uncompromised trust in software for the regulated, AI-powered world. Only Black Duck solutions free organizations from tradeoffs between speed, accuracy, and compliance at scale while eliminating security, regulatory, and licensing risks. Whether in the cloud or on premises, Black Duck is the only choice for securing mission-critical software everywhere code happens. With Black Duck, security leaders can make smarter decisions and unleash business innovation with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Regional Field Chief Technology Officer to serve as a senior technical executive, trusted advisor, and public voice of our technology strategy in the market. In this role, the Regional Field CTO will operate at the intersection of technology, sales, and the customer — engaging directly with C-level and technical leaders at our most strategic customer accounts, translating our AI-driven platform capabilities into credible technical narratives, and representing the company as a thought leader across the industry. This is a customer-facing, pre-sales technical leadership role reporting to the VP of Sales Engineering, with a dotted line to Product &amp;amp; Technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as trusted technical advisor and recurring executive sponsor for C-level and senior technical stakeholders at strategic, enterprise, federal and other key accounts — pivoting fluidly between business strategy conversations, risk, compliance, and deep technical architecture reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead highly visible, multidisciplinary technical engagements of strategic importance across the region, including executive briefings, architecture reviews, whiteboard sessions, customer advisory feedback loops, and partner or analyst-facing discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Black Duck as a technical evangelist for the platform and roadmap within a region, delivering keynotes, webinars, whitepapers, and thought leadership content at industry events, and representing the company externally with press, analysts, and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate Black Duck platform AI/ML, detection engine, and platform architecture capabilities into clear, credible narratives for both technical and executive audiences, speaking candidly to responsible AI practices such as data privacy, model governance, and human-in-the-loop controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Presales leadership on the region’s most strategic and enterprise opportunities, leading technical deep-dives, architecture reviews, whiteboard sessions, and executive briefings, and advising on the technical implications of new product launches, roadmap changes, and competitive positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support RFPs and security questionnaires with authoritative technical input, and articulate competitive and technical differentiation, including nuanced comparisons of AI/ML capabilities against alternatives in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively engage strategic accounts to strengthen technical trust, identify expansion opportunities, mitigate renewal risk, and guide customers toward secure software development and application security maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and solve problems of strategic or industry scope, using innovative approaches to remove technical barriers, strengthen customer confidence, and improve business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide field-informed guidance on emerging AI-assisted software development, agentic workflows, application security trends, and competitive market dynamics that may influence Black Duck strategy or customer adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture, synthesize, and escalate regional customer, partner, and market feedback into actionable input for Product, Engineering, and Sales systematically capturing technical objections and influencing the roadmap, packaging, launch readiness, and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, enable, and review technical storytelling by sales engineers and account executives, including how to explain AI features accurately without overclaiming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Experience Required&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years in a senior technical leadership role (CTO, Sales Engineering leader, Principal Architect, or equivalent), including several years in a customer-facing or field/pre-sales capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record engaging and influencing C-level and senior technical audiences at enterprise organizations, with demonstrated success across complex enterprise sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain expertise in application security (SAST, SCA, DAST), enterprise architecture, cloud/SaaS platforms, APIs and integrations, and security best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, practical understanding of AI/ML concepts as applied to security (e.g., anomaly detection, large language models, behavioral analytics, AI-assisted software development, agentic workflows), along with a candid grasp of their limitations and the practical limitations and controls needed for responsible adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success negotiating with and influencing executive leadership, significant customers, partners, analysts, or vendors to shape technical decisions and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to exercise wide latitude in determining objectives and approaches for complex, critical assignments with material regional, functional, or market impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping standards, methods, practices, or market-facing technical narratives within an industry or discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to translate complex technical concepts into clear stories for both executive and highly technical audiences, including customers, partners, press, analysts, and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated industry presence — conference speaking, published thought leadership, active contribution to industry/analyst communities, customer advisory leadership, or comparable external technical influence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, able to translate complex technical concepts for both technical and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel up to 50% to customer sites and industry events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Cybersecurity, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or other advanced degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Black Duck is an equal opportunity employer. We consider all applicants for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, religion, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, sexual orientation, veteran or military service status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law. Black Duck complies with all applicable laws prohibiting employment discrimination in every jurisdiction where it operates and provides reasonable accommodations to individuals with disabilities in accordance with applicable law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/blackduck/regional-field-cto-emea-germany-netherlands-france-italy-ireland-finland-sweden-37072","tags":["2030 - Sales Engineers (GQP)"],"job_types":[],"location":"EMEA, Germany, Netherlands, France, Italy, Ireland, Finland, Sweden)","created_at":1793699717},{"slug":"director-of-enterprise-ai-and-data-strategy-london-430757","company_name":"thoughtworks","title":"Director of Enterprise AI and Data Strategy","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;description content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Director-level Market Lead to head our Data &amp;amp; AI practice in the UK &amp;amp; Ireland. This is a hybrid leadership role. You combine deep technical solutioning with real commercial skill, and you are credible both in an architecture debate and across the table from a CDO, CIO or CFO.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our delivery model is shifting from large time-and-materials teams to small, AI-first pods working against a business outcome. As Market Lead, you will shape how we take that model to UKI clients: what we sell, how we price it, and how we staff and deliver it. You will lead a core team of 5–6 direct reports and a wider matrix of around 50-75 people across UKI, and you will help them build the skills this shift requires. We are developing these ways of working together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;job-responsibilities&quot;&gt;Job responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The successful candidate is a true dual-threat practitioner, equally at home in a complex architecture discussion and in closing a large commercial deal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive commercial success on complex Data &amp;amp; AI deals across UKI, from shaping the opportunity through to a signed deal. This includes structuring fixed-price and outcome-linked commercial models, and understanding delivery cost, margin and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with tech advisory and industry domain leads from pre-sale through delivery, so the commercial story, the architecture and the sector insight reinforce one another.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frame and test business-outcome hypotheses with executives, and define thin slices of delivery that prove value quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You stay close enough to delivery to know what is realistic, and you share accountability for outcomes on the deals you sell.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spearhead growth of the UKI Data &amp;amp; AI practice: build, lead, scale and mentor a high-performing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with delivery and talent leads to match demand with capacity, so the right people and pods are available when deals land. Keep specialist skills sourced and bench waste low.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shift the practice&#39;s capability mix towards production AI engineering and agentic delivery, through hiring, reskilling and role-based onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage executive-level relationships with CDOs, CIOs, CISOs and other CXOs. Act as a sparring partner on AI strategy: challenge assumptions, size the opportunity, and help clients decide where agentic automation and AI can move the P&amp;amp;L.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage robust sales pipelines and lead strategic client workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise clients on responsible AI, covering risk, governance and regulatory expectations in the UK and wider markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expected to lead and drive P&amp;amp;L with TCV of 50 -75 M GBP and ACV of 45-50 M GBP/&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expected experience and capabilities in driving all P&amp;amp;L criterias including sales, margin, utilization, bench management, training, learning, partnership based sales etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;job-qualifications&quot;&gt;Job qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;technical-skills&quot;&gt;Technical Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Enterprise Tech &amp;amp; AI Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep proficiency in at least one major cloud (GCP, AWS, Azure), modern data platforms (Snowflake, Databricks), and AI/NVIDIA ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Data/AI Production Experience (70/30 Split):&lt;/strong&gt; 15+ years in data consulting with concentrated recent depth (last 2–4 years) in productionizing AI, LLMs, and agentic systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Delivery &amp;amp; Risk Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep understanding of the realities of deploying AI into production—specifically evaluating failure modes, delivery costs, governance, and technical risks (not just drawing architecture diagrams).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Complex Deal Structuring:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven history of shaping and selling large-scale Data &amp;amp; AI deals, specifically transitioning clients to outcome-linked or fixed-price commercial models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;3,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;P&amp;amp;L &amp;amp; Operations Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Hard business acumen required to manage £50–£75M TCV and £45–£50M ACV, including driving margins, utilization, bench management, and capacity planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;professional-skills&quot;&gt;Professional Skills&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,0,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Suite Advisory &amp;amp; Presence:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional ability to act as a strategic sparring partner to CDOs, CIOs, and CFOs. Comfort challenging client assumptions and negotiating ROI and business cases at the executive level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,1,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Navigating Ambiguity:&lt;/strong&gt; High resilience and drive. The ability to build momentum and define strategy while internal delivery models, pricing structures, and competency frameworks are still maturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,2,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,2,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Consultative Facilitation:&lt;/strong&gt; Adept at framing business-outcome hypotheses, leading strategic client workshops, and breaking down massive transformations into thin, fast-value delivery slices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,3,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Matrix Leadership &amp;amp; Change Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience leading, scaling, and managing a matrixed team of 50–75 practitioners across the UKI region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p data-path-to-node=&quot;5,4,0&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-path-to-node=&quot;5,4,0&quot; data-index-in-node=&quot;0&quot;&gt;Coaching &amp;amp; Capability Building:&lt;/strong&gt; A strong mentoring mindset focused on reskilling existing talent, raising the overall AI fluency of the practice, and shifting the team towards AI-first delivery pods.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;important-things&quot;&gt;Other things to know&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;important-things content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;There is no one-size-fits-all career path at Thoughtworks: however you want to develop your career is entirely up to you. But we also balance autonomy with the strength of our cultivation culture. This means your career is supported by interactive tools, numerous development programs and teammates who want to help you grow. We see value in helping each other be our best and that extends to empowering our employees in their career journeys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;responsible-ai-use&quot;&gt;Responsible Use of AI in Recruitment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;responsible-ai-use content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;At Thoughtworks, we use AI tools to support our recruitment team with administrative tasks such as drafting communications, scheduling interviews and writing job descriptions.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Crucially, our AI tools do not screen, assess, rank or make hiring decisions. Every application is reviewed by our team and all selection decisions are made exclusively by our interviewers and hiring managers.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are committed to fairness and responsible AI. We actively manage our AI systems by testing, monitoring for biased outcomes and implementing mitigation measures. We hold our third-party vendors to these same high standards through a rigorous governance process. For additional information, please see our full &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thoughtworks.com/careers/ai-policy-for-recruitment&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Thoughtworks AI Policy for Recruitment&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;description content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about&quot;&gt;About Thoughtworks&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;Thoughtworks is a dynamic and inclusive community of bright and supportive colleagues who are revolutionizing tech. As a leading technology consultancy, we’re pushing boundaries through our purposeful and impactful work. For 30+ years, we’ve delivered extraordinary impact together with our clients by helping them solve complex business problems with technology as the differentiator. Bring your brilliant expertise and commitment for continuous learning to Thoughtworks. Together, let’s be extraordinary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 80px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-qualifications content&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;skills inner-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;display: none;&quot;&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.thoughtworks.com/careers/ai-policy-for-recruitment&quot;&gt;See here our AI policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/thoughtworks/director-of-enterprise-ai-and-data-strategy-london-430757","tags":["1Y_UKHLD SL DATA"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1793699716},{"slug":"product-integration-engineer-defence-bath-369775","company_name":"Distance Technologies","title":"Product Integration Engineer, Defence","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a <strong>Product Integration Engineer</strong> to develop and prove out our products with military customers, starting with the Field Operator HUD (FOH): a head-mounted, always-on visual intelligence system built from Distance hardware, a HUD operating system and AI-assisted data processing that pulls sensor, feeds and command-and-control into the operator's field of view. Your job is to make it work on a specific customer's platform, in the field, not just on a bench, as part of our core R&amp;D team. If you're a hands-on generalist who knows VR or XR and would rather be where the tech meets the user than stuck at a desk, this one's for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHY DISTANCE?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Distance Technologies, the problem we're solving is simple to state and hard to solve: the amount of data in the world is endless, but human capacity is not. We are building a fundamentally new perception layer between humans and machines, transforming transparent surfaces into interfaces unlike the world has ever seen. Think of the windscreen of a car, the visor of a helmet, or a sight device, each becoming a new front-end for AI. The way we turn bits and atoms into expanded human perception is protected by over 50 granted international patent families. We build it for two demanding worlds: defence and automotive. And we build it from a single foundation fusing software, hardware and computational optics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">There are 60 of us today, with decades-long experience building world's best products, optics, and open-source operating systems. We partner and build with globally leading companies like<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://distance.tech/news/distance-announces-collaboration-with-kia-integrating-new-panoramic-lightfield-hud-into-the-kia-vision-meta-turismo-concept-car"> <u>KIA</u></a>,<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://distance.tech/news/supacat-and-distance-technologies-sign-framework-agreement-to-enable-aerospace-grade-hud-capability-across-the-entire-supacat-hmt-ground-vehicle-platform"> <u>Supacat</u></a>, and<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://distance.tech/news/galvion-and-distance-collaborate-on-advanced-helmet-systems-with-distances-computational-optics-and-acuity-os"> <u>Galvion</u></a>, and we were Google Ventures' first investment in Finland.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>THE ROLE</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The FOH is already in field trials with military users. Your first project is getting it working with British Army equipment and defence primes, building the integration around what the customer actually needs. As our product line grows you'll take on a widening set of customer integrations across our defence work, each one a different platform, stack and set of interfaces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your core responsibilities include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owning customer integrations end to end.</strong> Make the FOH work inside a customer's platform: adapt the software, wire it into their sensors, displays, video and connectivity, and get it demo- and trial-ready. Prototype fast in dedicated environments to prove value with a client before it hits the shared codebase.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Being Distance in the field.</strong> Join demos, trials and exercises with defence clients, support on-site deployments when needed, and bring back what you see and hear on real kit.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bridging the field and the core.</strong> Turn what customers need into concrete integration work with the R&amp;D and commercial teams, spot what should become shared product capability, and feed it into the roadmap and, eventually, the shared codebase.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You won't be a satellite. You'll join the software standups and reviews and be a real part of R&amp;D.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHAT'S IN IT FOR YOU</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work ships and gets used. What you integrate goes into real kit already in trials with military users, and what you learn from demos, trials and exercises with them feeds straight back into the product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own the whole thread. From first prototype to working integration in the field, it's yours, not passed between five teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">New display tech. Glasses-free computational optics and a see-through HUD, the kind of problem you won't find at most XR jobs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A small team backed to move fast. Around 60 of us, Google Ventures' first investment in Finland, and flat enough that your calls count.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>OUR EXPECTATIONS</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What we're looking for:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A builder, not a passenger: a hands-on self-starter who takes ownership, works things out when docs are missing, and would rather be with a customer or in the field than at a desk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least a couple of years of software engineering experience with VR or XR, plus generalist instincts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort across a mixed software stack. You've worked with some of C++, Unity and embedded, and you pick up the rest quickly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some exposure to electrical integration or software-to-hardware interfaces. We're not expecting deep hardware experience on top of strong software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're at home in prototype and integration work: incomplete docs, customer-specific stacks, messy interfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good with clients, and happy to be the person representing Distance at a demo or trial.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willing to travel within the UK when needed, and to Finland now and then.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">It's a bonus, though not required, if you've worked with HMDs, wearable displays or spatial computing, know C++ for integration and application development, can stand up a UI or application stack for quick situational-awareness or demo prototypes, are comfortable with embedded or Linux at integration level, or have seen sensor, display and video interfaces at system level.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be based within commuting distance of the Bath office and in the office two to three days a week. Our working language is English.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>DID WE GET YOU INTERESTED?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply via the application form. Our recruitment process includes 2-3 discussions with the team. If you want to learn more about the position, reach out to our recruiter, Joel Kinnunen, at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="underline underline underline-offset-2 decoration-1 decoration-current/40 hover:decoration-current focus:decoration-current" ---------- Kindly note that, for data privacy reasons, we are not able to process applications sent via email.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We process your application data only for this recruitment and in line with applicable data privacy law.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/distance-technologies/product-integration-engineer-defence-bath-369775","tags":["Tech"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Bath, UK","created_at":1793698818},{"slug":"workplace-manager-uk-london-22285","company_name":"Trustly","title":"Workplace Manager - UK","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHO WE ARE </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Trustly, we're building a smarter, faster, and more secure financial future by revolutionizing the world of payments. As a global leader in Open Banking Payments, we are establishing Pay by Bank as the new standard at checkout, providing unparalleled freedom, speed, and ease to millions of consumers and merchants worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Ambition: To build the world’s most disruptive payment network and redefine what the payment experience should feel like.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trustly is a global team of innovators, collaborators, and doers.  If you are driven by a strong sense of purpose and thrive in a dynamic, entrepreneurial, and high-growth environment, join us and be part of a team that’s transforming the way the world pays.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Trustly, our employees are our users and the workplac