millions of people experience work, we'd love you on the team.<br /><br />Visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://www.perk.com">www.perk.com</a> to learn more.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div><div style="left:0px;width:100%;height:0px;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/4899a966-8724-4480-958f-7271e5dc2807/f3e1915d-e346-4987-a1fb-9c447e8786c0" style="top:0px;left:0px;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0px" allowfullscreen="true" scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perk works best when it connects seamlessly with the tools and platforms our customers</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">already rely on. From ERP and accounting systems to workplace software, mobility providers,</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">technology platforms, and emerging AI ecosystems, these third-party relationships can directly</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">shape the value customers get from Perk.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a <strong>Senior Manager, Product Partnerships </strong>to own and build those relationships.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlike our Growth Partnerships and Supplier Partnerships teams, this role isn’t responsible for</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">generating sales pipeline or supplier commission revenue. Its goal is to make Perk’s product</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">and customer experience stronger through the third parties we depend on and integrate with.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll determine where strategic relationships can unlock the most customer value, build and</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">manage those partnerships, secure the access and agreements our teams need, and work</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">closely with Product and Engineering to turn them into successful customer-facing experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a new role at Perk with significant opportunity to define how Product Partnerships should</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">work as we scale.<br /></p><h2><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build our product partnership strategy:</strong> Translate Perk’s product and company priorities into a clear roadmap of third-party relationships across areas such as ERP and accounting, business software, mobility, integration platforms, and AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own strategic partner relationships: </strong>Serve as Perk’s primary relationship owner for the external platforms and technology companies that enable or enhance customer-facing product experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlock Product and Engineering: </strong>Secure the developer access, API licences, programme memberships, certifications, marketplace approvals, and other partner support our teams need to build and maintain integrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Structure and negotiate partnerships:</strong> Lead commercial and strategic discussions around API access, data, licensing, marketplace participation, co-marketing, and other partnership terms, working closely with Legal, Security, Finance, Product, and Engineering.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Partner with Product on priorities:</strong> Bring the partner and market perspective into roadmap discussions while Product Managers own product requirements and delivery. Help determine which external relationships and integration models create the greatest customer value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the partner lifecycle: </strong>Manage relationships from initial engagement through integration, certification, launch, ongoing roadmap alignment, escalations, programme changes, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive adoption and customer value:</strong> Work with Product, Marketing, Customer Success, Sales, and Support to ensure partnerships aren’t simply launched—they are discoverable, useful, reliable, and adopted by customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"> <strong>Build the Product Partnerships playbook: </strong>Establish how Perk evaluates, prioritises, launches, measures, and manages product partnerships as this function grows.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in strategic partnerships, ecosystem partnerships, business development, or a product-adjacent role within SaaS, fintech, or B2B technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building and managing complex relationships with technology or platform companies, ideally including developer, API, certification, or marketplace programmes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working with Product and Engineering and understanding technical concepts such as APIs, OAuth, data models, sandboxes, and integration dependencies without needing to be an engineer.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to distinguish between an interesting partnership and one that will meaningfully improve Perk’s product or customer experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong relationship-building, negotiation, and communication skills across both external partners and senior internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to move complex initiatives forward across Product, Engineering, Legal, Security, Finance, Marketing, Customer Success, Support, and Sales without relying on direct authority.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable defining the strategy, operating model, priorities, and processes for a new function rather than inheriting an established playbook.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to build the case for a partnership and measure its impact through adoption, customer experience, integration quality, and other relevant outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based within commuting distance of our London or Barcelona hub.<br /> </p></li></ul><h2>Nice to Have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with ERP, accounting, spend management, payments, travel, or fintech ecosystems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing relationships with major business software, technology, mobility, or AI platforms.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with unified API or integration-platform models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with European ERP and accounting ecosystems across markets such as DACH, Benelux, France, the Nordics, or the UK.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional European languages.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What We Offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Receive competitive compensation and equity ownership in Perk</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rest and recharge with 25 days of annual leave plus bank holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take control of your physical health with private medical cover and voluntary dental insurance from Bupa, and discounted gym memberships with GymFlex</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan for your future with our qualifying earnings company pension plan with Aviva</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Know that your loved ones are protected financially through your Life Insurance if the worst were to happen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rest assured that you’re covered by income protection in case you experience a long-term sickness or absence</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leverage tax-efficient cycle and electric car schemes with Cycle2Work &amp; Octopus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join our unforgettable Perk events, including our spectacular annual summer party</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Always feel supported with Spring Health, our market-leading wellbeing partner, providing fast, comprehensive access to 12x therapy and 12x coaching sessions for you and your loved ones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Focus on your family with 12-16 weeks’ paid parental leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to your community with 16 paid hours per year to spend volunteering for your dearest charitable causes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Broaden your horizons with up to 20 "Work from Anywhere" days per year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay savvy with access to a wide variety of discounts and rewards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Follow your passions and take a four-week, fully paid sabbatical once you reach 5 years</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Let us help you move to one of our hubs with relocation support <br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>The Process </strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Talent Acquisition Interview - 30 mins - Virtual</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiring Manager Interview - 30 mins - Virtual </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assessment Interview - 60 mins - IRL / Virtual </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Values interview - 30 mins - Virtual</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Perk</strong><br />AI is embedded in how we work across every function. The tools you'll use day-to-day are AI-enabled so you can move faster and spend more time on the work that matters. In practice, that means using AI to research and prioritise accounts, draft and refine outreach, handle customer interactions more effectively, synthesise information, and cut through shadow work - the invisible tasks that pull people away from the work only they can do - so you can focus on relationships and outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How We Work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Perk, we take an IRL-first approach to work, where our team works together in-person 3 days a week. As such, this role requires you to be based within commuting distance of our hubs. We fundamentally believe in the value of meeting in real life to improve connectivity, productivity, creativity and ultimately making us a great place to work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For certain roles, we can help with relocation from anywhere in the world, English is the official language at the office. Please submit your resume in English if you choose to apply. Do not forget to submit an updated portfolio and/or resume.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perk is a global company with a diverse customer base, and we want to make sure the people behind our product reflect that. We’re an equal opportunity employer, which means you’re welcome at Perk regardless of how you look, where you’re from, or anything else that makes you, well, you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Protect Yourself from Recruitment Scams</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">All official communication from Perk will always come from email addresses ending in @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://perk.com">perk.com</a> or @<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://externalperk.com">externalperk.com</a>, our verified social media channels, or recruiters listed on our official LinkedIn page. We will never ask you to pay for equipment, training, or fees, request sensitive personal information such as bank details early in the process, or communicate through unofficial apps like WhatsApp, Telegram, or Signal. If you receive a message claiming to be from Perk that seems suspicious, please do not respond. Forward it to <u>security [at] perk .com</u>, and we will confirm whether it is legitimate.<br /><br />#LI-Hybrid</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/perk/senior-manager-product-partnerships-london-148829","tags":["Supplier Partnerships"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793688015},{"slug":"diesel-mechanic-london-30287","company_name":"Saronic Technologies","title":"Diesel Mechanic","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Saronic Technologies is a leader in revolutionizing autonomy at sea, dedicated to developing state-of-the-art solutions that enhance maritime operations through autonomous and intelligent platforms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Job Overview</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are currently seeking a skilled Diesel Mechanic to join our team. The successful candidate will be responsible for maintaining, repairing, and troubleshooting diesel engines and related systems on our autonomous surface vessels (ASVs) to ensure optimal performance and reliability.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Perform routine maintenance tasks on diesel engines, including oil changes, filter replacements, and fluid checks, to ensure proper functioning and longevity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diagnose and repair diesel engine malfunctions, mechanical issues, and electrical faults using diagnostic tools, technical manuals, and troubleshooting techniques.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Inspect and test diesel engine components, systems, and subsystems to identify and address potential problems or areas of concern.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Overhaul and rebuild diesel engines and associated systems, including fuel injection systems, turbochargers, and exhaust systems, as needed to restore performance and efficiency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate records of maintenance and repair activities, including parts used, labour hours, and service performed, to track equipment history and ensure compliance with maintenance schedules and regulatory requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Follow safety protocols and procedures for working with diesel engines and related equipment, including proper handling and disposal of hazardous materials and fluids.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with other maintenance technicians, engineers, and operators to troubleshoot complex problems, share technical knowledge, and implement effective solutions.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Qualifications</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Marine Diesel and/or Volvo VODIA experience required</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">GCSEs (or equivalent) are required. A recognised vocational qualification or apprenticeship in diesel mechanics, marine engineering, or a related discipline is preferred.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience as a diesel technician or a diesel mechanic, with demonstrated proficiency in diagnosing, repairing, and maintaining diesel engines and related systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong mechanical aptitude and technical skills, with the ability to read and interpret technical manuals, diagrams, and schematics.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with diagnostic tools and equipment used in diesel engine repair, such as scan tools, multimeters, and oscilloscopes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent problem-solving skills and the ability to troubleshoot complex mechanical and electrical issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Effective communication skills and the ability to work independently or as part of a team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness to work in a dynamic, fast-paced environment with changing priorities and deadlines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to travel as needed to meet business objectives, including throughout the Indo-Pacific region and to our headquarters in Austin, Texas. This role will require spending 30+ days training at Saronic headquarters in Austin, Texas. </p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Physical Demands</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to perform physically demanding work for extended periods.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Frequently and repetitively lift, push, and carry up to 23 kg's.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work outdoors for extended periods in marine and waterside environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Frequently and repetitively bend, lift, and reach to install and remove components of varying size and weight.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to stand and walk for extended periods, including over varied and uneven terrain such as docks, vessel decks, and gravel surfaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stoop, lay, bend, reach, squat, kneel, crouch, twist, and crawl for extended periods while working in confined or low-clearance spaces.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Climb and maintain balance on ladders, platforms, vessels, and other elevated structures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to loud noise, vibration, engine exhaust, and hazardous materials with required adherence to safety and disposal procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wear Personal Protective Equipment at all times in work areas, including safety glasses, gloves, hearing protection, steel-toed footwear, and other PPE as required.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Benefits</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stock Options:</strong> Equity options to give employees a stake in the company’s success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive Salary:</strong> Industry-standard salaries with opportunities for performance-based bonuses</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Medical Insurance:</strong> Comprehensive private health insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time Off: </strong>Generous annual leave entitlement, plus public holidays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Parental Leave:</strong> Paid maternity and paternity leave to support new parents</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>This role requires the legal right to work in the United Kingdom. Employment may also be subject to applicable security, export control, and government contracting requirements.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>If this role is based in the United States, it requires access to export-controlled information or items that require “U.S. Person” status. As defined by U.S. law, individuals who are any one of the following are considered to be a “U.S. Person”: (1) U.S. citizens, (2) legal permanent residents (a.k.a. green card holders), and (3) certain protected classes of asylees and refugees, as defined in </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="postings-link" href="https://www.govinfo.gov/link/uscode/8/1324b"><em>8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3)</em></a><em>.</em><br /><br />Saronic does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. <em><u>We are also committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities.</u></em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/saronic-technologies/diesel-mechanic-london-30287","tags":["Mission Ops"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1793688014},{"slug":"commercial-contracts-associate-nda-london-117750","company_name":"Norm Ai - Commercial Contracts Associate (NDA)","title":"Commercial Contracts Associate (NDA)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Norm Ai</strong><br />Norm Ai, the agentic law company, has a client base with a combined $30 trillion in assets under management.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Norm Ai pioneered Legal Engineering, the process that empowers lawyers to build and supervise domain-specific AI agents with Norm’s proprietary suite of no-code software tools. Norm Ai technology is deployed inside many of the largest and most consequential institutions in the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Norm Ai is also the technology behind Norm Law, LLP, a separate but affiliated AI-native law firm built for the era of agentic AI. Norm Law’s attorneys advise leading institutions across private funds, private equity, venture capital, real estate, registered funds, and financial regulation, using the same legal intelligence platform that powers Norm Ai’s products.<br /><br /><strong>AI Fluency:</strong><br />Norm Ai prefers all team members to be fluent in AI. Successful candidates actively use AI in their day-to-day work to support thinking, creation, and problem-solving. They use it to improve the quality and speed of their work and to continuously refine how work gets done end-to-end.<br /><br />Candidates should be prepared to demonstrate and discuss their AI usage throughout the interview process, including concrete examples of tools, workflows, and outcomes. We look for practical, hands-on experience, not theoretical familiarity.</p><h3></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>This Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Commercial Contracts Associate (NDA), you will work on a high impact team that provides important services to Norm Law’s clients, while using AI agents to streamline the drafting, review, and execution process in providing non-disclosure agreement review for clients. You’ll collaborate closely with partners, clients, and technology teams to deliver efficient, precise, and data-driven legal services for in-house legal teams of leading asset managers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our practice embraces the use of AI to reduce burden and increase your ability to focus on strategic legal judgment and client engagement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Document Drafting, Review, and Negotiation:</strong> Leverage AI agents to generate, compare, negotiate, and redline NDAs tailored to client guidelines</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Incorporating Legal Context:</strong> Advise clients on their NDA playbooks and market standards, including ensuring AI agents understand each client's specific context and comparing client’s actual practices with playbook positions in order to guide updates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>NDA Execution:</strong> Integrate AI agents into workflow management, execution, negotiation, and coordination with counterparties for any NDAs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Client Advisory:</strong> Partner with clients to demonstrate how AI-assisted workflows improve accuracy, transparency, and velocity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration with Tech:</strong> Work closely with the technology teams to continue to make the NDA review process even more efficient using AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Managing high volumes of requests:</strong> Maintain a tracker, manage multiple high priority requests simultaneously and communicate timing expectations to clients and consistently and proactively follow up and move negotiations forward. </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><h3><strong>Core Qualifications</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Qualified solicitor admitted in England and Wales, with a current Solicitors Regulation Authority (SRA) practising certificate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2-3+ years of experience reviewing NDAs or similar agreements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong drafting and communication skills; meticulous attention to detail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interest in applying technology to enhance traditional deal workflows.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What Success Looks Like</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>30 Days:</strong> Learn firm AI platforms; begin supporting the commercial contracts team using AI-enabled review and drafting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>60 Days:</strong> Independently manage discrete components of NDA review with AI support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>90 Days:</strong> Lead AI-augmented workstreams in live NDA reviews, improving efficiency and accuracy in document management and execution processes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong> pension plan with an employer contribution, medical and dental insurance coverage, employee referral bonus program, initial 2 week onboarding in the US.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Work Location</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Central London</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work model:</strong> Hybrid</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In-office expectation:</strong> 4-5 days per week</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why Join Norm Law</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be part of the founding UK team bringing a proven US category leader to a receptive UK market.  You’ll have autonomy, visibility, and the opportunity to build meaningful relationships — backed by a world-class product, an experienced executive team, and a growing global reputation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To learn more about Norm Ai, visit our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.norm.ai"><strong>website</strong></a>.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/norm-ai-commercial-contracts-associate-nda/commercial-contracts-associate-nda-london-117750","tags":["Norm Law"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793688014},{"slug":"infrastructure-engineer-united-kingdom-465744","company_name":"Augmodo","title":"Infrastructure Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">At Augmodo, we are expanding our global footprint and building a follow-the-sun engineering model. Currently, our core infrastructure team is based in the US Bay Area. As our customer base and engineering cohorts grow internationally—particularly across Europe and Australia—we need an infrastructure engineer stationed in the EU/EMEA time zone.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will be the anchor for our European engineering cohort, drive system reliability, and serve as the infrastructure lead during EU business hours. You’ll balance active incident response and system maintenance with long-term infrastructure building.</p><h3>Key Responsibilities</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the primary infrastructure contact during EU working hours, extending coverage to support cross-regional needs in APAC (AUS) and EMEA.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build, scale, and optimize infrastructure dedicated to supporting our growing EMEA teams and regional customer deployments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively manage system health, monitoring, alerting, and incident response for GCP-based workloads to maintain high availability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automate deployments, manage Kubernetes clusters, and build internal tooling that empowers developers to ship code safely and fast.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish effective async workflows and handoff protocols with other infrastructure teams to ensure seamless 24/7 continuity.</p></li></ul><h3>Core Qualifications</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience as a software engineer in a production environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor's degree in computer science, engineering, or math.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of hands-on experience running and scaling workloads in Google Cloud Platform (GCP).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of experience managing production Kubernetes clusters (GKE experience is a big plus).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in Python and Go for building infrastructure automation, APIs, and operational tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience with Infrastructure as Code (Terraform/Pulumi), CI/CD pipelines, and observability tools (Prometheus, Grafana, Datadog, etc.).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High degree of self-direction and clear async communication skills, with experience thriving in distributed team environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with hosting, serving, or orchestrating agentic AI systems and LLM workflows.</p></li></ul><h3>Nice