&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-JW1&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/catonetworks/enterprise-sales-director-paris-paris-167480","tags":["Enterprise Sales Director - EMEA"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris, Paris","created_at":1793710520},{"slug":"products-analytics-engineer-internship-paris-444018","company_name":"Ledger","title":"Products Analytics Engineer - Internship","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a team of experts pushing the limits of what’s possible, united by our common goal to unlock true freedom through digital ownership, making technology accessible for all. We believe in a world where users, creators and enterprises manage their value with ownership and freedom. Our curiosity drives us to innovate, empowering individuals on a global scale. We believe change is constant and our team moves forward as one, with a culture of problem-solving where every employee is empowered and supported to challenge tradition and create solutions. Our mission is simple: to make self-custody accessible and give people the keys to their own financial futures. If you want to make a true impact, we want you to join us at Ledger.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Ledger, we’re proud to be the global platform for digital assets and Web3, with over 20% of the world’s crypto assets secured through our Ledger devices. With our headquarters in Paris, and offices in Vierzon, Grenoble, Montpellier, London, Portland, Geneva, Zurich and Central Singapore, we have a team of around 600 professionals developing a variety of products and services to enable individuals and companies to securely buy, store, swap, grow and manage crypto assets – including the Ledger hardware wallets line with more than 7.5 millions units already sold in 200 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Product Analytics Engineer Intern, you will join the Product Analytics team supporting Ledger Wallet across Product, Business, and Growth/CRM teams. Reporting directly to the Product Data Analytics Manager, you will play a key role in ensuring tracking data quality, and scaling our analytics infrastructure to support company-wide data-driven decision-making.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration:</strong> Work closely with Product Managers, Data Engineers, and Data Scientists to deliver insights and support Growth/CRM personalization pipelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experimentation &amp; A/B Testing:</strong> Specify and support A/B test setups, funnel evaluation, and advanced statistical analysis for product features.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI Governance &amp; Automation:</strong> Help establish governance, guardrails, and custom skills for users querying analytics platforms (Mixpanel, Snowflake MCP) via AI tools, and contribute to building end-to-end AI-assisted tracking workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tracking Quality &amp; Investigations:</strong> Triage, investigate, and follow up on tracking issues to maintain data sanity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Documentation &amp; Enablement:</strong> Develop comprehensive documentation and data models (dbt/data mart) to empower stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Privacy &amp; Compliance:</strong> Maintain standard privacy-aware constraints across all data modeling and analytics workflows.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final-year student in Engineering, Computer Science, Data Science, or a related technical field seeking an end-of-studies internship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong proficiency in SQL, Python scripting, and data modeling concepts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Analytics engineering mindset with a focus on data quality, reliability, reproducibility, and documentation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of A/B testing methodologies, statistical analysis, and funnel evaluation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Product Analytics tools (e.g., Mixpanel, Amplitude) and data visualization tools is a strong plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience or deep curiosity regarding AI agents and workflow automation is a strong plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interest in Web3, digital assets, and crypto is a plus.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Ledger, we are dedicated to continually investing in our employees which is why we offer more than just salaries; we provide comprehensive compensation packages that include a wide range of benefits. Here are some of the benefits you can look forward to:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexible work options - </strong>Our hybrid policy allows employees to work from home up to 3 times per week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health &amp; Wellness support - </strong>Health and Life Insurance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial growth opportunities - </strong>Employees can become shareholders in Ledger as well as other financial benefits depending on your country of work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commuter allowance - </strong>Ledger offers a commuter allowance to contribute to your preferred means of transportation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; Development </strong>- A comprehensive suite of training solutions providing a personalised learning experience for every employee.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">For regionally specific benefits, your Talent Acquisition contact will be able to provide you with more information.<br /><br /><em>We’re committed to building an inclusive hiring process. If you need any adjustments or accommodations, just let us know, we’ll do our best to support you.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/ledger/products-analytics-engineer-internship-paris-444018","tags":["Corporate Functions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris, France","created_at":1793709616},{"slug":"principal-thermo-mechanical-engineer-paris-grenoble-422857","company_name":"Vinci","title":"Principal Thermo-Mechanical Engineer- Paris/Grenoble","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are building <strong>Physics AI for hardware design</strong>. Our software platform helps hardware designers and physics simulation engineers explore, analyze, and optimize hardware systems, leveraging cutting-edge AI to deliver ultrafast, accurate physics intelligence within the realities of engineering design workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our first product bridges the gap between the accuracy &amp; determinism of traditional simulation and the speed &amp; scaling of AI, and is redefining how the world’s most advanced semiconductors are designed, verified, built,  brought to market and integrated in complex systems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Role Overview</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a pivotal leader within our <strong>European Forward Deployment team</strong>, you will drive the <strong>adoption of Vinci’s platform </strong>among the region's top engineering organizations. In this strategic role, you will <strong>build, mentor, and guide </strong>a high-performing team of thermal engineers dedicated to engaging prospective customers and demonstrating our software's transformative value.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As <strong>trusted technical advisors</strong>, you and your team will use deep simulation expertise to help enterprise customers <strong>validate and optimize complex, real-world designs</strong>. Through these collaborative engagements, you will champion Vinci's value proposition by showing how our platform delivers systemic improvements in thermal performance, product reliability, and time-to-market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leveraging strong fundamentals in<strong> continuum mechanics</strong>, you will guide analyses of complex physical phenomena, including linear, geometric and material nonlinearities, and contact interactions. Your team will <strong>evaluate critical factors</strong> such as <strong>warpage, stress evolution, thermal cycling, and reliability across advanced semiconductor devices, electronics packages, and wafer-scale systems.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work closely with <strong>customer engineering teams</strong> to understand their technical challenges, provide expert guidance, and clearly articulate Vinci’s capabilities in solving real-world problems. You will also serve as a <strong>key feedback channel t</strong>o product and engineering teams, translating customer insights into actionable inputs that shape product direction and drive continuous improvement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a <strong>remote role, </strong>with close collaboration with Sales, Product, and Engineering in Palo Alto, CA, USA. The role includes <strong>moderate travel</strong>, primarily within continental Europe. Some <strong>infrequent intercontinental travel </strong>may be required for discussions and collaboration with the US team<strong>.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build, lead, and scale a high-performing team of thermo-mechanical engineers</strong>, setting the technical direction, hiring, mentoring team members, and driving field execution across Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborate closely with the sales team</strong> to lead technical discussions, scope proof-of-concept (PoC) evaluations, and deliver compelling product demonstrations to prospective enterprise customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Guide customer engineering teams through the evaluation phase</strong> by overseeing simulation setup, running complex test cases, and interpreting results to explicitly prove Vinci’s technical and business value.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own customer enablement through onboarding, deployment pipeline and account expansion</strong>, providing senior technical guidance, structured training sessions, and advanced troubleshooting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Provide product guidance and feedback, identify customer pain points and workflow bottlenecks</strong>, partnering directly with internal product and engineering teams to transform field feedback into critical new product features.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Represent Vinci at major industry conferences and semiconductor events</strong>, engaging technically with key prospects and partners through technical presentations and live platform demonstrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain a strong understanding of <strong>competitive technologies, industry trends, and market positioning</strong> to communicate Vinci’s differentiators effectively.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Qualifications (Minimum Qualifications)</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Education:</strong> Degree in Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related technical field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical depth:</strong> Expert-level mastery of commercial FEA software (e.g., Ansys Mechanical, Abaqus, or equivalent), with 15+ years of hands-on experience in thermo-mechanical simulations— either as a practitioner running simulations or as a technical account manager for commercial physics simulation software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Industry Domain:</strong> Deep familiarity with semiconductor electronics packaging, advanced packaging technologies (e.g., 2.5D/3D IC), or foundry ecosystems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Engagement:</strong> Prior experience in dedicated customer-facing roles, with a strong ability to build trust and manage engineering client relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Automation &amp; Scripting:</strong> Practical programming experience using Python or C++ to automate workflows or parse simulation data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leadership Impact:</strong> Proven track record of prior managerial or technical leadership experience, with the ability to scale, mentor, and drive execution across engineering teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication:</strong> Elite interpersonal and communication skills, with a proven ability to distill complex physics and simulation results into clear, high-impact narratives for both deep technical panels and business-oriented executives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred (Desirable Differentiators)</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Multiphysics Breadth:</strong> Familiarity with thermal management and cooling solutions and/or Electrical Signal Integrity and Power Integrity (SI/PI) workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercial Track Record:</strong> Direct experience commercializing technical software—ideally electronic design automation (EDA) or CAE simulation tools—into major semiconductor and electronics enterprises.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Go-To-Market Experience:</strong> Prior experience explicitly within technical pre-sales, application engineering (FAE), or strategic technical sales environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Emerging Tech Adjacency:</strong> Ability to rapidly adopt and champion next-generation, physics-based workflows and AI-assisted design or simulation tools.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why Join Us</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not just use AI; be part of a team actively redefining how next-generation silicon and hardware are architected.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work at the absolute convergence of state-of-the-art AI models, fundamental physics, and high-stakes enterprise engineering.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with world-class engineers and researchers in a fast-moving startup environment.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>À propos de Vinci</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vinci développe une IA fondée sur la physique (Physics AI) pour la conception de systèmes hardware. Notre plateforme donne aux équipes de conception et de simulation des prédictions physiques précises, obtenues en une fraction du temps d'une simulation classique, et qui s'intègrent à leurs outils existants.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">C'est la première solution à offrir à la fois la rigueur de la simulation traditionnelle et la vitesse de l'IA. Elle transforme la façon dont les semi-conducteurs les plus avancés au monde sont conçus, vérifiés, fabriqués, mis sur le marché et intégrés dans des systèmes complexes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Présentation du poste</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">En tant que membre clé de notre équipe européenne de Forward Deployment, vous jouerez un rôle déterminant dans l'adoption de la plateforme Vinci par les principales organisations d'ingénierie de la région. Dans ce rôle stratégique, vous constituerez, accompagnerez et dirigerez une équipe performante de spécialistes en ingénierie thermique, chargée d'accompagner nos clients et prospects et de démontrer concrètement la valeur de notre logiciel.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">En tant que référent technique de confiance auprès de nos clients, vous et votre équipe mettrez à profit votre expertise approfondie en simulation pour aider nos clients industriels à valider et optimiser des conceptions complexes dans des conditions représentatives de leurs applications réelles. À travers ces collaborations, vous démontrerez comment la plateforme Vinci permet d'améliorer les performances thermiques et la fiabilité des produits, tout en accélérant les cycles de conception et la mise sur le marché.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Grâce à votre solide maîtrise de la mécanique des milieux continus, vous guiderez l'analyse de phénomènes physiques complexes : comportements linéaires, non-linéarités géométriques et matérielles, et interactions de contact. Votre équipe aidera les clients à évaluer des paramètres critiques tels que le warpage, l'évolution des contraintes, le cyclage thermique et la fiabilité, sur des composants semi-conducteurs avancés, des packages électroniques et des systèmes à l'échelle du wafer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vous travaillerez en étroite collaboration avec les équipes d'ingénierie de nos clients afin de comprendre leurs problématiques techniques, de leur apporter une expertise approfondie et de démontrer clairement comment Vinci peut répondre à leurs cas d'usage concrets. Vous jouerez également un rôle essentiel d'interface entre les clients et nos équipes Product et Engineering, en transformant les retours du terrain en informations exploitables pour orienter la feuille de route produit et contribuer à l'amélioration continue de la plateforme.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ce poste est basé en France et exercé en télétravail, avec une collaboration étroite avec les équipes Sales, Product et Engineering basées à Palo Alto, en Californie. Il implique des déplacements réguliers mais modérés, principalement en Europe continentale, ainsi que des déplacements occasionnels aux États-Unis pour collaborer avec l'équipe américaine.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsabilités</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Construire, diriger et développer une équipe performante d'ingénieur/es en thermomécanique, en définissant l'orientation technique, en recrutant et accompagnant les membres de l'équipe, et en pilotant l'exécution sur le terrain à travers l'Europe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborer étroitement avec l'équipe Sales pour diriger les discussions techniques, définir le périmètre des évaluations en proof-of-concept (PoC) et réaliser des démonstrations de produits convaincantes auprès de clients industriels potentiels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accompagner les équipes d'ingénierie des clients pendant la phase d'évaluation en supervisant la mise en place des simulations, l'exécution de cas de test complexes et l'interprétation des résultats afin de démontrer concrètement la valeur technique et business de Vinci.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Piloter l'accompagnement technique des clients, notamment l'onboarding, le déploiement et l'expansion des comptes, en fournissant une expertise technique de haut niveau, des sessions de formation structurées et un support avancé pour la résolution des problèmes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fournir des orientations et des retours sur le produit, identifier les difficultés rencontrées par les clients et les points de friction dans leurs workflows, et collaborer directement avec les équipes Produit et Engineering internes afin de transformer les retours du terra