potheses as quickly as possible</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuing to sharpen our view of where the value is and which markets and business models are accessible to us</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building lasting relationships with grid operators and the regulator, so that Axle is well positioned as the market evolves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as the conduit between partners and engineering, creating fast, structured feedback loops that turn field insights into product improvements</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">As such, we are looking for a “full-stack operator” who can process highly technical information, ramp up commercial value, and accelerate us into new markets.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You might have previous experience in one or more of the activities above, but we are more interested in your growth potential than your domain-specific expertise. We are looking for people who have built things, developed new relationships, and helped get big projects over the line in complex environments.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an opportunity to deliver first-of-a-kind projects in one of Europe’s most important flexibility markets, become a domain expert, and work at the bleeding edge of electrification.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What’s in it for you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a 12 month fixed-term contract. Ideally, you would be able to start by February 2027.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compensation is highly competitive and dependent on experience.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We operate with a deliberately flat structure and aim to keep pay equitable across the company, with a 1:1 median ratio between founder and team compensation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bi-annual retreats to strengthen team connection &amp; shared purpose.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be based in the France. To maximise collaboration, we ask that you spend ~1 week per month working from our London office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The opportunity to directly shape the future of energy markets and accelerate the transition to a low-carbon world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are <em>extremely</em> keen to build a diverse team, and we’re particularly eager to hear from candidates who don't fit the traditional role stereotypes. If you’re motivated by our mission, please do reach out, even if you feel you might not ‘check all the boxes’.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Interview process</h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take-home exercise</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final interview (in-person)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer, references, and welcome to the team!</p></li></ol><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/axle-careers/international-expansion-paris-234476","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"France","created_at":1793709614},{"slug":"enterprise-customer-success-france-445720","company_name":"2501","title":"Enterprise Customer Success","description":"<h2>About 2501</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">2501 builds autonomous AI agents that operate directly in the shell to complete real production tasks - not just synthetic evals. We treat LLMs as pluggable brains, mixing open‑source and flagship models to get the best result. By fusing their output with observability data we surface root causes fast and automate the dull parts of incident response for corporate engineering teams who can’t afford downtime.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a tight‑knit team of DevOps, Platform, and Infra engineers who ship fast, learn constantly, and elevate each other every day.</p><h2>Why 2501 ?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">