nspruchsvolle Mandate und mit der Zeit z.B. die technische Leitung von UiPath-Mandaten. Deine Zertifizierungen hältst du mit unserem Weiterbildungsbudget aktuell und baust sie weiter aus.</p><p>Konkret:</p><ul><li><p>Du baust Testautomatisierung mit der UiPath Test Suite bei unseren Kunden auf und integrierst sie in CI/CD-Pipelines.</p></li><li><p>Du bringst Agentic-Testing-Ansätze mit UiPath in Kundenprojekte ein.</p></li><li><p>Du berätst Kunden bei Toolauswahl, Architektur und Automatisierungsstrategie.</p></li></ul><h2>Das bringst du mit</h2><ul><li><p>Du verfügst über mehrere aktuelle UiPath-Zertifizierungen, darunter mindestens eine auf Professional-Level, z. B. Automation Developer Professional oder Test Automation Engineer Professional.</p></li><li><p>Du hast 2-3 Jahre Praxiserfahrung mit UiPath, vor allem in der Testautomatisierung, und hast Lösungen eigenständig umgesetzt.</p></li><li><p>Du hast Erfahrung in der Beratung von Kunden und Stakeholdern, kommunizierst fliessend auf Englisch und Grundkenntnisse in Deutsch, die du weiter ausbauen möchtest.</p></li><li><p>Du bist bereit, in der gesamten Deutschschweiz bei Kunden vor Ort zu arbeiten.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Das bringst du idealerweise zusätzlich mit</strong></p><ul><li><p>UiPath Agentic Automation Associate oder weitere Zertifizierungen aus dem UiPath-Portfolio</p></li><li><p>ISTQB Foundation Level oder weiterführende ISTQB-Zertifizierungen</p></li><li><p>Erfahrung mit CI/CD-Umgebungen wie Azure DevOps, GitLab oder Jenkins</p></li><li><p>Grundkenntnisse in C# oder VB.NET</p></li><li><p>Erfahrung mit weiteren Testtools wie Tricentis Tosca oder Playwright</p></li></ul><h2>Deine ersten Monate bei Infometis</h2><p>Du startest nach Vereinbarung in eine unbefristete Anstellung mit drei Monaten Probezeit. Je nach Projekt arbeitest du schon früh direkt beim Kunden. Dabei hast du ein Team im Rücken, das dich stärkt. Bei Fragen helfen sich die Infometen und Infometinnen untereinander schnell und unkompliziert, auch über Projekte hinweg.</p><h2>Wie sieht der Bewerbungsprozess aus?</h2><p>Bis Ende November sammeln wir alle Bewerbungen und sehen sie uns sorgfältig an. Im Dezember starten wir mit den Interviews. Passt dein Profil, melden wir uns bei dir für einen Termin. Schick uns deine Bewerbung deshalb am besten bis <strong>Ende November</strong>.</p><h2>Benefits</h2><ul><li><p>Sozialleistungen: Du profitierst von überdurchschnittlichen Sozialleistungen.</p></li><li><p>Work-Life-Balance: Geniesse eine 40-Stunden-Woche, die dir genug Raum für Leben neben der Arbeit lässt.</p></li><li><p>Weiterbildungsbudget: Dank einem grosszügigen jährlichen Weiterbildungsbudget bringst du deine Skills auf das nächste Level und kannst dich persönlich weiterentwickeln.</p></li><li><p>Gadgets: Bleibe technisch up-to-date mit einem jährlichen Budget für Gadgets.</p></li><li><p>Team-Events: Von abwechslungsreichen Teamaktivitäten über das Weihnachtsessen bis hin zu unseren regelmässigen Co-Working Days oder Qarterlies: Gemeinsam stärken wir den Zusammenhalt und leben den einzigartigen Infometis-Vibe.</p></li><li><p>Infowell: Profitiere von unserem internen Programm für Betriebliches Gesundheitsmanagement inklusive Plattform für mentale Gesundheit.</p></li><li><p>Zufriedenheit grossgeschrieben: Als «Kununu Top Company 2027» geben wir weiter alles für ein Arbeitsumfeld, in dem du dich wohl fühlst.</p></li></ul><p></p><p></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/infometis-ag/test-automation-engineer-uipath-zurich-440417","tags":["Quality Assurance","Inspection"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","berufserfahren"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1793709155},{"slug":"projektleiter-in-projektierung-aarau-263953","company_name":"two.jobs","title":"Projektleiter/in Projektierung","description":"<p>Im Auftrag unseres Kunden <strong>Husistein & Partner AG</strong> suchen wir eine/n <strong>Projektleiter/in Projektierung</strong></p><p>Wir brauchen Verstärkung!</p><p>Du suchst ein spannendes und dynamisches Arbeitsumfeld, wo Du Dich weiterentwickeln kannst? Du willst mehr Verantwortung und Entscheidungen treffen? Du arbeitest zielorientiert und hast hohe Qualitätsansprüche? Dann bist Du bei uns genau richtig! Unser Team plant anspruchsvolle Projekte.</p><p><strong>Deine Aufgaben:</strong></p><ul><li>Konzeptionelles Kreieren von Projekten in der Projektierungsphase</li><li>Führen von internen Projektteams</li><li>Sicherstellung der qualitativen und kosteneffizienten Projektbearbeitung</li><li>Sicherstellung der Vertragserfüllung</li><li>Koordination zwischen Büro und externen Beteiligten</li><li>Sicherung der Schnittstelle für nachfolgende Planungsphasen</li><li>Baurechtliche Sicherstellung der Bewilligungsfähigkeit von Bauprojekten</li></ul><p><strong>Deine Skills:</strong></p><ul><li>Erfahrung in den Phasen SIA 102 und im Projektierungsmanagement</li><li>Selbständige Projektführung</li><li>Führungserfahrung und gute kommunikative Fähigkeiten</li><li>Zuverlässigkeit, Belastbarkeit und Engagement</li><li>Gute Kenntnisse von ArchiCAD</li><li>Verhandlungssicheres Deutsch in Wort und Schrift</li></ul><p><strong>Unser Angebot für Dich:</strong></p><ul><li>Eine abwechslungsreiche und herausfordernde Stelle</li><li>Hohe Selbstständigkeit</li><li>Unterstützung durch unser Admin-Team</li><li>Möglichkeit zur Weiterentwicklung</li><li>5 Wochen Ferien, ein moderner Arbeitsplatz in einem digitalen Umfeld</li><li>Kollegiale Bürokultur, die für Eigenverantwortung, Professionalität und Menschlichkeit steht</li></ul><p>Genau was Du suchst? Dann sind wir gespannt auf Deine komplette Bewerbung als PDF-File an ----- z.Hd. Monika Reinhard.</p><p>Bitte stelle uns mit deinem Lebenslauf auch deine <strong>Zeugnisse und Diplome</strong> zu. Herzlichen Dank vorab!</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/twojobs/projektleiter-in-projektierung-aarau-263953","tags":["Project Management"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag"],"location":"Aarau","created_at":1793341870},{"slug":"research-engineer-index-intelligence-zurich-383448","company_name":"Exa","title":"Research Engineer, Index Intelligence","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Exa is an applied AI lab building a search engine unlike the world has ever seen. We build massive-scale infra to crawl the entire web, train state-of-the-art embedding models to process it, and design super high performant vector databases to retrieve over it. We now power search for Cursor, Cognition, HubSpot, and over 400,000 developers and have raised $350m from Lightspeed, Benchmark, and a16z.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ultimate goal is to build perfect search over all the world's information, far beyond Google. If you want to build massive-scale ML systems that will define the way the new AI world consumes information, this is the place for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We crawl the web continuously and cannot keep all of it, refresh all of it, or spend a GPU on all of it. Something has to decide which pages are worth indexing, which links are worth following, which pages say the same thing as pages we already have, what has gone stale, and what we should never have picked up. These decisions are worth more than most ranking work. The cheapest way to improve search is to stop indexing pages nobody should ever retrieve, and to start indexing the ones we are missing. Today they run on a mix of learned signals and thresholds someone picked.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a research engineer to own the signals behind those decisions, and the decisions themselves.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Desired Experience</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable owning a problem with no ground truth, where the first job is defining what the right answer means</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on ML experience with classifiers, rankers and calibration, plus strong data instincts at web scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You think in end-to-end impact. A signal only counts if a decision changes and search gets better</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You like working across teams. Crawling, indexing and retrieval all consume what you build</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You care about the problem of finding high quality knowledge and recognize how important this is for the world</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Example Projects</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make parsing work on the pages where it currently does not, and prove the improvement rather than assert it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teach a model to judge page quality, and get everyone to agree on what quality means well enough to supervise it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on credibility and misinformation as a modelling problem: what a page claims, whether it is a reliable source of it, and whether it was written for a reader or for a crawler</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide whether two documents are semantically the same or genuinely different, so we can deduplicate the web without collapsing pages that a user would want to see separately</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exa is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related conditions, criminal histories consistent with applicable law, or any other basis protected by applicable law.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/exa/research-engineer-index-intelligence-zurich-383448","tags":["Research"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1793331617},{"slug":"research-engineer-content-understanding-zurich-338885","company_name":"Exa","title":"Research Engineer, Content Understanding","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Exa is an applied AI lab building a search engine unlike the world has ever seen. We build massive-scale infra to crawl the entire web, train state-of-the-art embedding models to process it, and design super high performant vector databases to retrieve over it. We now power search for Cursor, Cognition, HubSpot, and over 400,000 developers and have raised $350m from Lightspeed, Benchmark, and a16z.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ultimate goal is to build perfect search over all the world's information, far beyond Google. If you want to build massive-scale ML systems that will define the way the new AI world consumes information, this is the place for you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a backend engineer, you'd play a critical role in our search architecture. We're pretty flexible on what projects people work on based on their skills and interests.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Search quality is bounded by what we understand about a page. Before anything can be retrieved, something has to work out what the page actually says. That means parsing it into the parts that are content and the parts that are furniture, classifying what kind of page it is and what it is about, telling whether the page is usable at all, extracting when it was published, judging how good it is and whether it can be trusted, and working out whether it says anything that a page we already have does not. All of this has to work on every page on the web, in every language, in every shape the web comes in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some of this is classic document understanding. Some of it is much more open. Credibility and misinformation, AI-generated and machine-spun content, and pages written to be found rather than read are all unsolved, and search results are only as trustworthy as our answers to them.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a research engineer to work on this. There is a lot of room to do it well.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Desired Experience</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Graduate-level ML experience (Master’s or PhD with at least 2 years of relevant experience), or an exceptionally strong undergrad</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can build a transformer from scratch in PyTorch, and you have trained models that then had to be cheap enough to run everywhere</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You like building large-scale datasets and living in the data. Most of the wins here are in the supervision rather than the architecture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable with problems where the ground truth does not exist yet and defining it is part of the job</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You care about the problem of finding high quality knowledge and recognize how important this is for the world</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Example Projects</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make parsing work on the pages where it currently does not, and prove the improvement rather than assert it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teach a model to judge page quality, and get everyone to agree on what quality means well enough to supervise it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work on credibility and misinformation as a modelling problem: what a page claims, whether it is a reliable source of it, and whether it was written for a reader or for a crawler</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Decide whether two documents are semantically the same or genuinely different, so we can deduplicate the web without collapsing pages that a user would want to see separately</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build classification and extraction that is accurate at web scale and cheap enough to run on all of it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design the supervision for something nobody has labels for, and find out whether it is learnable at all</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Trace a bad search result back to the page-level prediction that caused it, and fix it at the source</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exa is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related conditions, criminal histories consistent with applicable law, or any other basis protected by applicable law.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/exa/research-engineer-content-understanding-zurich-338885","tags":["Research"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1793331617},{"slug":"software-engineer-knowledge-engine-query-engine-zurich-49685","company_name":"Exa","title":"Software Engineer, Knowledge Engine – Query Engine","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Exa is an applied AI lab building a search engine unlike the world has ever seen. We build massive-scale infra to crawl the entire web, train state-of-the-art embedding models to process it, and design super high performant vector databases to retrieve over it. We now power search for Cursor, Cognition, HubSpot, and over 400,000 developers and have raised $350m from Lightspeed, Benchmark, and a16z.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ultimate goal is to build perfect search over all the world's information, far beyond Google. If you want to build massive-scale ML systems that will define the way the new AI world consumes information, this is the place for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Knowledge Platform team builds Exa's knowledge engine. We continuously synthesize information from across the web and beyond into one of the world's largest open-domain knowledge graphs, with hundreds of billions of evidence-backed claims. The work has two halves: construction pipelines that decide what to trust, and retrieval engines that decide how best to search it. Our goal is to give agents answers to any factual question about the world with unprecedented precision and completeness.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you'll own the <strong>query engine</strong> that searches hundreds of billions of claims across a variety of retrieval backends, from a distributed graph database to vector, full-text, time-series and geospatial indexes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is greenfield work with a massive scope. No off-the-shelf system answers precise questions over hundreds of billions of evidence-backed claims at agent speed, so you'll make foundational decisions, from storage layout and indexing across engines to the query language and the planner that routes work between them, that every query depends on.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own storage and indexing across backends:</strong> data layout, partitioning and indexes for graph, vector, full-text, time-series and geospatial retrieval, with bulk snapshot builds and live ingest that never take the system down.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Decide how best to search:</strong> cost-based planning from cardinality estimates that chooses, for each question, which backends to use, in what order and how to join their results, executed as traversals, retrievals, filters and aggregations in one plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make it fast at scale:</strong> serve thousands of queries per second, profiling and cutting p50/p99 latency, memory and cost per query under high concurrent load, from on-disk layout to network fan-out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keep answers consistent while the data converges:</strong> the graph is fed by live updates and bulk snapshots at once and is eventually consistent by design, so you'll own what a query may see while it converges: consistent snapshot promotion, ordered application of live updates and stable pagination across versions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measure precision and completeness:</strong> end-to-end checks every deployment must pass, plus evals and metrics that show when a plan returns wrong results or misses ones it should have found.</p></li></ul><h2>What we're looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've worked deep inside a distributed database, query engine, search engine or storage system.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong grasp of indexing, query planning and optimization, and storage formats.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid grasp of distributed systems fundamentals: consensus, replication, sharding and fault tolerance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong in a systems language (Go, Rust or C++).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You profile before you optimize, and you've shipped measured latency wins in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You obsess over correctness, reliability and data quality as much as scale.</p></li></ul><h2>Bonus</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Graph databases, or combining vector, full-text, time-series and geospatial retrieval</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compilers, query language design or cost-based optimizers</p></li></ul><h2>Example projects</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a system that retrieves and reasons over everything known about any company or person in the world, answering any factual question precisely and completely.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Answer precise multi-hop questions over hundreds of billions of claims at thousands of QPS with interactive latency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a planner that picks the right mix of graph, vector, full-text and geospatial retrieval for any question, and proves it chose well.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make new knowledge queryable seconds after it's synthesized, without ever serving an inconsistent result.</p></li></ul><h2>Logistics</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> This is an in-person opportunity in Zurich.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Visas:</strong> We're happy to sponsor international candidates (e.g., STEM OPT, OPT, H1B, O1, E3). While we cannot guarantee your visa, we have historically been successful in sponsoring candidates from all over the world. If you receive an offer, our team will work hard to get you a visa.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong> We offer premium healthcare benefits (medical, dental, vision), fertility benefits, 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave for all new parents, and a monthly wellness stipend to all of our employees.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exa is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related conditions, criminal histories consistent with applicable law, or any other basis protected by applicable law.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exa is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, disability, age, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related conditions, criminal histories consistent with applicable law, or any other basis protected by applicable law.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/exa/software-engineer-knowledge-engine-query-engine-zurich-49685","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1793331617},{"slug":"remote-director-of-strategic-accounts-407977","company_name":"tanium","title":"Director of Strategic Accounts","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Basics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
