, and recommendations</strong> for technical accuracy, financial consistency, completeness, and sound business judgment</p></li><li><p><strong>Identify material errors, unsupported assumptions, inconsistencies, and weaknesses</strong> in financial models or conclusions</p></li><li><p><strong>Define clear evaluation criteria and acceptable outcomes</strong>, accounting for valid alternative financial approaches and reasonable assumptions</p></li><li><p><strong>Write precise task instructions, reference answers, and concise executive-level explanations</strong> that accurately reflect the underlying financial analysis</p></li><li><p><strong>Apply structured evaluation guidelines consistently</strong>, providing clear, evidence-based rationales for your assessments</p></li></ul><p>The project focuses on developing and evaluating realistic financial tasks to assess how effectively advanced AI systems can perform complex FP&A workflows. Your role is to bring practical financial expertise to the design of challenging business scenarios and the evaluation of AI-generated outputs against professional standards.</p><h2>Requirements</h2><p><strong>You're a strong candidate if you:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Have 5+ years of relevant professional experience</strong> in Financial Planning & Analysis (FP&A), corporate finance, finance business partnering, or a closely related field, or equivalent demonstrated expertise</p></li><li><p><strong>Have advanced Excel and financial modeling skills</strong>, including building, reviewing, and auditing complex financial models with transparent formulas and well-documented assumptions</p></li><li><p><strong>Have hands-on experience owning or supporting financial planning processes</strong>, including operating budgets, rolling forecasts, variance analysis, headcount planning, and investment evaluations</p></li><li><p><strong>Have a strong understanding of financial statements and accounting principles</strong>, including the income statement, balance sheet, cash flow, working capital, liquidity, and debt covenants</p></li><li><p><strong>Are comfortable building scenario-based financial models</strong>, evaluating different business assumptions, and assessing their impact on financial performance</p></li><li><p><strong>Can independently reconcile complex or conflicting financial information</strong> across spreadsheets, contracts, business documents, and management reports</p></li><li><p><strong>Have strong analytical judgment</strong> and can identify material financial errors, flawed assumptions, inconsistencies, and unsupported conclusions</p></li><li><p><strong>Can assess the quality and correctness of financial analyses</strong>, including recognizing valid alternative methodologies and defining clear acceptance criteria</p></li><li><p><strong>Have excellent written English communication skills</strong> and can produce precise instructions, structured financial explanations, and concise executive memos</p></li><li><p><strong>Have strong attention to detail</strong> and can consistently apply detailed evaluation guidelines while exercising independent professional judgment</p></li></ul><p><strong>Preferred qualifications:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Experience in <strong>software, technology, or SaaS businesses</strong>, including ARR, retention, gross margin analysis, and subscription-based financial planning</p></li><li><p>Experience with <strong>financial model auditing, quality assurance, or reviewing financial deliverables</strong> prepared by others</p></li><li><p>Previous exposure to <strong>AI evaluation, benchmark development, or designing structured analytical assessments</strong></p></li><li><p>Experience presenting financial analyses and recommendations to senior management or executive stakeholders</p></li></ul><h2>Benefits and Compensation </h2><ul><li><p><strong>$400 USD per accepted task</strong>, with an estimated completion time of 5–6 hours</p></li><li><p>Fully remote and flexib