to 800V DC, combining ultra-compact SiC-based AC/DC and DC/DC power blocks. As we scale from Alpha customer readiness toward Production and Volume Readiness, securing the right components at the right price and lead time – power semiconductors, magnetics, PCBs and mechanical parts – becomes mission-critical.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Procurement &amp; Supply Chain Lead, you will own the purchasing and supply chain for the materials, equipment, parts and services that keep our prototype, pilot and volume production on track – from negotiating with suppliers to coordinating with contract manufacturers and logistics partners. You will partner closely with Engineering to translate technical requirements into sourcing decisions, and help build our purchasing processes as we scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is for you if you’ve negotiated with component suppliers yourself, like being hands-on, and enjoy building processes rather than following them – ideally with experience buying electronic components for B2B hardware such as power electronics, industrial equipment or automation systems. It isn’t for you if you prefer managing a team, require an established ERP and approval chain to work well, or a clearly defined, stable scope. It would not be a fit if your procurement background is mainly consumer goods, retail or indirect spend without hands-on exposure to electronic components.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contract and purchase raw materials, equipment, tools, parts, services and supplies needed for prototype, pilot and volume production.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Negotiate pricing, terms and delivery schedules with suppliers for critical components – power semiconductors, magnetics, PCBs, and mechanical/enclosure parts.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Issue and manage purchase orders; track order status and expedite as needed to meet production schedules.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Source and coordinate with suppliers and contract manufacturers (EMS, PCB vendors, logistics partners) on order status, lead times and quality issues.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with Engineering to understand technical requirements, communicate them clearly to suppliers, and identify alternate sourcing options for critical or long-lead-time components.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support supplier qualification and specification compliance for new and existing vendors.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain purchasing records, the Bill of Materials (BOM) and sourcing data; track lead times, inventory levels and supplier performance, and flag supply chain risks.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive logistics and inbound/outbound shipments together with our logistics partners.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scale the supplier base and purchasing processes as we move from Alpha Customer readiness to Production and Volume Readiness.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">BSc in supply chain management, business administration, engineering or comparable education, or equivalent experience.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Several years of hands-on experience in procurement, purchasing or supply chain, specifically in electronics or hardware manufacturing.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong negotiation skills; track record of managing supplier contracts and pricing.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Specific experience sourcing electronic or mechanical components (semiconductors, PCBs, magnetics, enclosures); experience with contract manufacturers (EMS) is a plus.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organised and detail-oriented, comfortable managing multiple supplier relationships.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team player, comfortable working cross-functionally with Engineering and Operations in a fast-paced start-up environment with evolving priorities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English, spoken and written; German language skills helpful, but not mandatory.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Equity + competitive salary.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unique technology and market opportunity – validated prototype and first paying customers on the path to volume shipments.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid work with flexible working times.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/hyperscale-power/procurement-supply-chain-lead-zurich-447215","tags":["Product & Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1793277640},{"slug":"head-of-solution-consulting-rd-field-cso-zurich-442239","company_name":"Benchling","title":"Head of Solution Consulting R&D / Field CSO","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are rebuilding biotech for the AI era.<br /><br />When a breakthrough is delayed, the world waits. Getting a molecule from discovery to patients, or a crop from lab to field, involves thousands of slow, manual, disconnected steps. AI has the potential to change this, compressing decades of R&amp;D work into years. But that only happens when clean, structured scientific data and AI are built into how science gets done.<br /><br />Benchling is the AI platform for biotech R&amp;D. Scientists use Benchling to design experiments, capture structured data, and run AI agents and models directly in their workflows. Over 200,000 scientists around the world trust Benchling to power their most important work, from academic labs to Sanofi, Moderna, and more than half of the world's top 50 biopharma.<br /><br />We’re building an AI scientist for our customers. We can’t do that if we haven’t built the muscle ourselves. AI fluency is the foundation we build on; it's core to how we work, and we're committed to helping every new hire integrate it into their day-to-day. As part of our interview process, you'll complete a brief AI-focused exercise or discussion so we can understand how you think about and use AI to drive impact in your role. Feel free to reference any tools, platforms, or workflows you use today.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>WHY THIS ROLE, WHY NOW</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">R&amp;D leaders trust people who have done the science. More than half of the world's top 50 biopharma companies already use Benchling, and many of the most important are in Europe. Our ambition is 10x faster science, from idea to first dose. With Science Foundries, launched at Benchtalk 2026, agents and scientists run entire R&amp;D workflows together, so a three-person team can have the productive capacity of thirty.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In a senior R&amp;D role, you can change how one organisation does science. As our Field CSO, you'll take one question to R&amp;D organisations across EMEA: how do we get from idea to first dose 10x faster?<br /></p><h2><strong>ROLE OVERVIEW</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll lead our EMEA R&amp;D Solution Consulting organisation: a team of 12, with two first-line leaders covering our Enterprise and Strategic segments, plus occasional support for APAC deals. You'll be the scientific counterpart to our General Manager, EMEA, and work alongside our Field CTO. They lead on IT, data science and architecture; you lead on the scientists and how their work changes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><h2><strong>RESPONSIBILITIES</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the scientific voice in the room.</strong> Brief the GM and account teams before key meetings, then join them as a peer to the CSOs and Heads of R&amp;D across the table. Act as senior sponsor on our largest EMEA opportunities, and use account-team introductions to open new R&amp;D relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead the 10x conversation.</strong> Turn Benchling's vision, from AI agents to Science Foundries, into a credible plan R&amp;D leaders can act on, including how their scientists move onto Benchling and what changes in the lab.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead and develop two first-line leaders</strong> and their team of 10. Provide in-region leadership continuity, set the scientific bar for every customer engagement, and build a succession plan as the team grows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Shape EMEA strategy and the roadmap.</strong> Decide with sales leadership where to focus the team's expertise, and bring patterns from the field back to Product, Marketing and global Solution Consulting.</p></li></ul><h3>HOW WE'LL MEASURE SUCCESS</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a commercial role with a scientific core. We'll look at EMEA revenue growth and influenced pipeline, technical win rate, forecast accuracy on the technical side of deals, regional ownership of our largest R&amp;D relationships, and the strength of your leadership bench.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><h2>QUALIFICATIONS</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Substantial hands-on R&amp;D experience in biotech or pharma, with a PhD or equivalent scientific depth. You've run experiments, led programmes and know how large R&amp;D organisations make decisions and adopt change.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A record of driving change, from adopting new technologies to rethinking how your teams work, and clear views on how AI will change R&amp;D.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading through other managers, and executive presence with VPs, Heads of R&amp;D and C-level leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial ambition and a growth mindset. We'll teach you how software is sold. We can't teach how a large R&amp;D organisation works from the inside, and that's what you bring.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Readiness for a field role: frequent on-site time with the largest pharma and biotech companies across EMEA, plus US travel three to four times a year for team offsites and our global sales kickoff.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English; German or French is a plus.</p></li></ul><h3>NICE TO HAVE</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Benchling or a comparable R&amp;D platform (ELN, LIMS or R&amp;D data platform), including leading its evaluation or rollout</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer-facing scientific, internal consulting, or CRO/CDMO programme leadership roles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Presales or solution consulting experience</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><h2>HOW WE WORK</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer a flexible hybrid work arrangement that prioritizes in-office collaboration. Employees are expected to be on-site 3 days per week (Monday, Tuesday, and Thursday).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-Hybrid </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#BI-Hybrid </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benchling welcomes everyone.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe diversity enriches our team so we hire people with a wide range of identities, backgrounds, and experiences. <br /><br />We are an equal opportunity employer. That means we don’t discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We also consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law, including but not limited to the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/benchling/head-of-solution-consulting-rd-field-cso-zurich-442239","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich, Switzerland","created_at":1793277638},{"slug":"senior-avaloq-engineer-wertschriftenabwicklung-50-zurich-30151","company_name":"Callista Group AG","title":"Senior Avaloq Engineer – Wertschriftenabwicklung 50%","description":"<p>Unser Kunde entwickelt und betreibt die Avaloq Core Banking Plattform im Bereich Anlagen &amp; Vorsorge nach dem DevOps-Ansatz. Als Teil eines grossen Agile Release Trains (ART) arbeitet das Team nach SAFe und SCRUM an strategischen Vorhaben und der kontinuierlichen Weiterentwicklung der Applikationslandschaft.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Zur Verstärkung des Teams suchen wir einen erfahrenen Avaloq-Spezialisten, der seine Expertise in der Parametrisierung und Weiterentwicklung der Plattform einbringt.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Hauptaufgaben:</strong></p><ul><li><p>Selbständiges Implementieren von Anforderungen aus dem Fachbereich auf dem vorgegebenen Technologie-Stack (Java Spring Backend, Angular</p></li><li><p>Parametrisierung und Weiterentwicklung d