&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/hsogroupbv/ai-platform-engineer-veenendaal-211691","tags":["03. AP - NL"],"job_types":[],"location":"Veenendaal","created_at":1793310919},{"slug":"enterprise-account-executive-iii-netherlands-71815","company_name":"Camunda","title":"Enterprise Account Executive III - Netherlands","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Camunda is <strong>the enterprise platform for agentic orchestration</strong>, enabling organizations to coordinate <strong>AI agents, people, and systems </strong>across complex, end-to-end business processes. With built-in governance, auditability, and human oversight, Camunda gives enterprises the control they need to move AI from pilots to production — safely and at scale. <strong>Trusted by over 700 organizations worldwide</strong>, including 9 of top 10 US banks, Camunda helps enterprises boost operational efficiency, accelerate time-to-value, and deliver better customer experiences.<br /><br /><strong>Fully remote and global,</strong> we are in the middle of something bigger: <strong>transforming into an AI-first organisation, built on our own platform</strong>. We use Agentic AI to automate, orchestrate intelligent processes, and elevate human contribution across every team.<br /><br />Named <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.gpbullhound.com/articles/top-100-next-unicorns-the-uk-france-and-germany-lead-with-the-most-promising-technology-companies-in-europe/"><u>GP Bullhound’s Top 100 Next Unicorn list,</u></a> <strong>2025 Great Place to Work certified.</strong> <em><strong>Visionary</strong></em><strong> </strong>in <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://page.camunda.com/wp-2025-gartner-magic-quadrant-for-boat"><strong><u>2025 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™</u></strong></a><strong> </strong>for Business Orchestration and Automation Technologies. ranked <strong>3rd in Flexa's 2026 </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://flexa.careers/companies/camunda"><strong>Most Flexible Companies</strong></a>, We’re growing fast and looking for top talent to join our team. <strong>If you want meaningful work, visible impact and put something genuinely rare on your CV, keep reading.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for an Enterprise Account Executive to build Camunda’s Dutch Government market. This is a territory-building role for a disciplined, consultative seller who can create demand, shape strategic opportunities, and guide complex buying groups through to executive-level decisions. You will own the full sales cycle across a focused set of government accounts, from account strategy and first conversation through business case, procurement, negotiation, close, and expansion.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will combine commercial ownership with public-sector credibility. The successful candidate will be comfortable engaging senior civil servants, CIO and transformation leaders, procurement, security, architecture, and business stakeholders. You will translate government priorities into a compelling value case for process orchestration, automation, and agentic workflows, while navigating formal procurement processes and the governance expectations of public-sector customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will own</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the Dutch Government territory and create a clear account and coverage strategy across priority national and public-sector organizations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain a healthy, self-generated pipeline, targeting at least 2.5x pipeline coverage through focused outbound activity, executive engagement, partner collaboration, and market development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop relationships across complex buying groups, including CIOs, CTOs, transformation leaders, enterprise architects, process owners, procurement, security, legal, and executive sponsors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the full enterprise sales cycle: discovery, qualification, value engineering, technical evaluation, business case, procurement, commercial negotiation, and close.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply MEDDICC consistently to create deal clarity, strengthen qualification, identify gaps early, and improve forecast reliability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build business cases connected to public-sector outcomes such as service quality, operational efficiency, transparency, resilience, compliance, and cost control.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate account teams across Solutions Engineering, Customer Success, Professional Services, Marketing, Product, Legal, Finance, and leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Developa partner-first motion with relevant global system integrators, regional partners, and public-sector specialists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expand successful customer relationships by identifying adjacent processes, departments, agencies, and use cases after the initial land.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain accurate account, contact, opportunity, and forecast data in Salesforce as the single source of truth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share market intelligence on government priorities, procurement dynamics, competitors, partners, and customer needs to improve Camunda’s Dutch public-sector go-to-market strategy.</p></li></ul><h2>What success looks like</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First 30 days</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a working understanding of Camunda’s platform, value proposition, sales methodology, customer evidence, pricing approach, and public-sector references.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Align with internal stakeholders on territory priorities, account ownership, partner coverage, and available sales resources.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Produce an initial account segmentation and stakeholder-mapping plan for the Dutch Government territory.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish a repeatable operating cadence for pipeline creation, deal inspection, forecasting, and cross-functional account-team collaboration.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First 90 days</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complete strategic account plans for the highest-priority government accounts, including business priorities, buying groups, whitespace, partners, competition, and next actions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create qualified pipeline through a balanced mix of net-new opportunities, partner-sourced activity, executive introductions, and expansion plays.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop a strong network of relevant government and ecosystem stakeholders, with clear relationship and meeting objectives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrate consistent MEDDICC qualification and accurate Salesforce hygiene across active opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify the most relevant public-sector use cases and value narratives for Camunda’s Dutch market development.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First 180 days and beyond</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish a credible, repeatable pipeline engine for the Dutch Government market.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Progress strategic opportunities through well-defined qualification, value validation, technical evaluation, procurement, and commercial stages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Win new government logos and create expansion paths into additional departments, agencies, or processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build trusted relationships with executive sponsors and public-sector ecosystem partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute actionable market insight that improves Camunda’s positioning, messaging, partner strategy, and investment decisions in the Netherlands.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver against quota while protecting long-term customer value, adoption, and expansion potential.</p></li></ul><h2>What you will bring</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must-haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of success in a quota-carrying enterprise software or SaaS Account Executive role, owning complex deals end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated experience selling into the Dutch Government or another highly regulated public-sector environment, with a clear understanding of formal procurement, security, legal, and governance requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of creating pipeline through proactive outbound activity and converting multi-stakeholder opportunities into material, preferably multi-year, contracts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong command of MEDDICC or a comparable enterprise sales methodology, with the discipline to qualify rigorously, manage mutual action plans, and forecast accurately.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Executive presence and communication skills in Dutch and English, with the ability to connect operational problems to strategic, financial, and citizen-impact outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A collaborative, customer-focused, and resilient approach aligned with Camunda’s FAITH values and global-first way of working.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selling process automation, workflow, orchestration, integration, business transformation, or adjacent enterprise technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Existing relationships across Dutch ministries, executive agencies, municipalities, provinces, public-service organizations, or government-focused partners.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with global system integrators, regional implementation partners, or public-sector framework agreements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Camunda, BPMN, DMN, process orchestration, cloud platforms, or agentic automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience creating quantified value cases for service modernization, compliance, operational resilience, or cost reduction.</p></li></ul><h2>Why this role matters now</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dutch public-sector organizations are under pressure to modernize services, improve efficiency, operate securely, and coordinate increasingly complex technology and regulatory environments. Process orchestration gives them a way to make that complexity visible and manageable while connecting people, systems, and automation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is an opportunity to shape a market rather than inherit a mature patch. You will have the ownership and visibility to define where Camunda can create the greatest public value, build the ecosystem around those opportunities, and establish a durable foundation for growth in the Netherlands.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join a global, distributed team that values initiative, transparency, customer impact, and practical collaboration. The role offers the chance to work at the intersection of public-sector transformation, enterprise technology, process orchestration, and the next generation of agentic automation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>This role is an existing vacancy</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-AG1 #LI-Remote </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We Have to Offer:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer competitive, fair, and transparent compensation. Salary ranges are location-based, with Standard and Major markets (global tech hubs) reflecting local competition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Annual Total Target Cash </strong>(base salary + 100% variable target, where applicable) shown below spans from the minimum in a Standard market to the maximum in a Major market. Final offers depend on <strong>skills</strong>, <strong>experience</strong>, and <strong>location</strong>, and we typically hire in the first half of the range to allow room for growth:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">United States: $281,300.00 to $453,500.00 </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">United Kingdom: £176,600.00 to £290,500.00 </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Singapore: S$349,400.00 to S$524,000.00</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re based elsewhere, you’ll be hired via <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Remote.com"><strong><u>Remote.com</u></strong></a> (our global employer partner), and your Talent Acquisition Partner will provide a personalized <strong>Total Rewards Calculator</strong> after your first interview.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equity: </strong>We also offer equity (where applicable) through our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hoyQAPTZ5nV7J47D9n3yqK5hhLj160Xf36iyqEXNOWE/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.2qon7r4kdfe1"><strong><u>Virtual Stock Option Plan (VSOP)</u></strong></a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits &amp; Perks</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We invest in your wellbeing, growth, and ability to connect, along with perks that support you no matter where you’re based. Our benefits are globally designed and locally delivered where applicable.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Remote &amp; Flexible: </strong>Work from anywhere with the setup that suits you, <strong>home office budget, co-working space support, and flexible time off</strong> to recharge when you need it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In Person Connection:  </strong>We invest in meaningful face time through our <strong>Annual Kickoff </strong>(Vienna in 2025, Madrid in 2026!), <strong>team offsites, and Camundi Connection Budgets</strong>, including contributing to meetups while travelling,, and local gatherings with fellow Camundi.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health &amp; Wellbeing:</strong> Access locally tailored healthcare, <strong>Modern Health</strong> for global mental wellbeing, and our <strong>Live Well Lifestyle Spending Account (LSA),</strong> a flexible, global benefit that puts you in control of your whole life, not just work, from: <strong>staying active, to caring for family, exploring personal passions, meaningful experiences, and investing in your financial wellbeing.</strong> The Live Well program launches in 2026 and scales to <strong>€1,000 annually from 2027</strong>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Financial Security:</strong> Retirement and pension plans (often with company contributions), plus life and disability insurance where relevant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Professional Growth:</strong> Up to $/€/£1,000 per year for self-driven learning: courses, certifications, books, you decide!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI in our hiring process</strong>:<em><strong> </strong>Camunda may use AI tools to aid the screening of applications and during the interview process. You can </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://camunda.com/ai-in-our-interviewing-process/"><em><strong>learn more here</strong></em></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>”Everyone is welcome at Camunda” </em>— <em>it’s a celebrated component of our culture. We strive to create an inclusive environment that empowers our people. At Camunda, we honour diverse cultures and backgrounds and are proud to be an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration without regard to gender, race, ethnicity, religion, belief, sexual orientation, age, disability or any other protected characteristics under applicable law. We are looking forward to your application!</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Come join us and be part of Camunda’s incredible journey: Make an impact at a pivotal moment in our story!</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Please be aware that scammers may impersonate Camunda by reaching out about job opportunities. Camunda will only contact candidates from an email address ending in @</strong></em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://camunda.com"><em><strong>camunda.com</strong></em></a><em><strong> or </strong></em><strong>@</strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://camunda.com"><strong>talent.camunda.com</strong></a><em><strong>. We will never ask candidates for bank account details, checks, payment, or other sensitive financial information as part of our hiring process. If you receive a suspicious message, please do not respond, click any links, or share personal information.</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Note for recruiting and placement agencies: Camunda does not accept unsolicited agency resumes. Please do not forward resumes to our careers site, employees, or any other Camunda contact unless we have specifically engaged your firm for that search. Camunda will not pay fees related to unsolicited resumes.</strong></em><br /><br />For information about how your personal data is processed, please refer to Camunda’s <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://legal.camunda.com/privacy-and-data-protection#applicant-privacy-policy"><u>Applicant Privacy Policy</u></a>. We note that phone numbers and SMS opt-in data are not shared, sold, or rented to third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional purposes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">By opting in to SMS use, please be aware that:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Text message frequency may vary;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Standard text message and data rates may apply; and</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">By opting in, you will be enrolled directly in ongoing recruiting text messages from Camunda.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">To opt-out, simply select 'No' when prompted during your application. You can also change your preferences at any time by contacting ----- style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/camunda/enterprise-account-executive-iii-netherlands-71815","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Netherlands","created_at":1793310017},{"slug":"technical-account-manager-benelux-netherlands-105423","company_name":"Camunda","title":"Technical Account Manager - Benelux","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Camunda is <strong>the enterprise platform for agentic orchestration</strong>, enabling organizations to coordinate <strong>AI agents, people, and systems </strong>across complex, end-to-end business processes. With built-in governance, auditability, and human oversight, Camunda gives enterprises the control they need to move AI from pilots to production — safely and at scale. <strong>Trusted by over 700 organizations worldwide</strong>, including 9 of top 10 US banks, Camunda helps enterprises boost operational efficiency, accelerate time-to-value, and deliver better customer experiences.<br /><br /><strong>Fully remote and global,</strong> we are in the middle of something bigger: <strong>transforming into an AI-first organisation, built on our own platform</strong>. We use Agentic AI to automate, orchestrate intelligent processes, and elevate human contribution across every team.<br /><br />Named <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.gpbullhound.com/articles/top-100-next-unicorns-the-uk-france-and-germany-lead-with-the-most-promising-technology-companies-in-europe/"><u>GP Bullhound’s Top 100 Next Unicorn list,</u></a> <strong>2025 Great Place to Work certified.</strong> <em><strong>Visionary</strong></em><strong> </strong>in <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://page.camunda.com/wp-2025-gartner-magic-quadrant-for-boat"><strong><u>2025 Gartner® Magic Quadrant™</u></strong></a><strong> </strong>for Business Orchestration and Automation Technologies. ranked <strong>3rd in Flexa's 2026 </strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://flexa.careers/companies/camunda"><strong>Most Flexible Companies</strong></a>, We’re growing fast and looking for top talent to join our team. <strong>If you want meaningful work, visible impact and put something genuinely rare on your CV, keep reading.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Camunda, our Technical Account Managers (TAMs) are trusted technical advisors, partnering closely with our most strategic customers to help them turn their process orchestration vision into measurable business value. In this highly impactful role, you’ll be “in the boat together” with clients from day one – navigating technical challenges, providing expert guidance, and ensuring smooth adoption of our platform at scale. Success means building lasting relationships, accelerating customer outcomes, and making complex technology feel approachable for diverse teams. If you thrive on collaboration, love solving unique challenges, and are excited to empower companies across industries, we want you on our fast-growing, innovative Customer Success team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the primary technical contact and trusted advisor for designated enterprise customers, leading them through all stages of their Camunda adoption journey</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide the creation and execution of tailored technical adoption plans, designed to maximize business outcomes and ensure long-term success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver hands-on technical guidance, best practices, and advisory services to both business and technical stakeholders – from onboarding through ongoing operations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify and remove execution risks by proactively conducting platform and solution health checks, facilitating escalation management, and advocating for customer needs internally</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Foster strong, collaborative relationships with cross-functional Camunda teams such as Customer Success Managers, Consulting, Support, Product, Engineering, Sales and Pre-Sales to drive measurable customer outcomes at scale</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regularly spend time on-site with accounts for key milestone interactions (as needed, up to 50% during busy periods) to deepen partnerships and accelerate strategic initiatives</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Bring to the Role</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 3 years of experience as a Technical Account Manager or a directly comparable role in enterprise software</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated technical expertise: hands-on with a high-level programming language (such as Java, C#, or Python) and relevant enterprise software frameworks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of modern solution architectures and associated paradigms, including DevOps topics (especially Kubernetes)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proven track record of building trusted relationships and providing advisory services to both technical and business stakeholders—able to synthesize and explain complex</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">issues clearly to varied audiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strategic problem solving competencies with a collaborative, impact-driven mindset; comfortable tailoring approaches to unique customer situations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Willingness and flexibility to spend time on-site with clients as account needs dictate (up to 50% during busy periods)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />Nice to Haves:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in enterprise automation, business process management, process orchestration, or robotic process automation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Relevant industry certifications (AWS Certified Solutions Architect, Azure Solutions Architect Expert, CKAD, CKA, etc.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with Camunda products</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability and/or willingness to use <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="external-link" href="https://accounts.cloud.camunda.io/signup?_ga=2.47330343.127558761.1654184528-504024057.1654184528">our product</a>.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-to-haves:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in enterprise automation, business process management, process orchestration, or robotic process automation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1