t-313287","tags":["Software Development","Remote"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1793298667},{"slug":"remote-ios-developer-utrecht-289501","company_name":"Luscii","title":"iOS Developer","description":"<p>At Luscii, we work on several applications within the OMRON Digital Health Circle, including the Luscii Thuismeten app and OMRON Connect. Together with our colleagues, we build technology that takes the burden off patients and healthcare professionals, creating more space for care. As an iOS Developer, you will help make this happen by building and improving the mobile applications that connect people, devices and healthcare.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>We create technology to make healthcare more accessible, as our digital health solutions help healthcare professionals monitor patients remotely, so people can receive the right care in the right place. As an iOS Developer, you will help us build and improve the mobile applications that make this possible.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Your work goes beyond writing code. You will help shape technical direction, share your expertise with colleagues and explore new technologies that can improve our apps. At Luscii, our Holacratic way of working also gives you the autonomy to take initiative, pick up responsibilities and contribute beyond your core role.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>The applications you build need to work reliably in a healthcare context, where stability and usability matter. You are going to make sure that our apps remain performant, scalable and easy to maintain, while exploring new ways to improve the experience for patients and healthcare professionals. By combining solid engineering with thoughtful technical choices, you will help us continue to develop its digital healthcare platform.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Your role</h3><p>As iOS Developer at Luscii, you will combine hands-on development with technical ownership, working closely with colleagues across development, QA and support to build, improve and maintain our applications. You turn ideas into useful, intuitive digital health solutions. Whether you are exploring a new technology, building a proof of concept or solving a production issue, you will have the autonomy to make technical decisions and the opportunity to influence how we build our apps.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>What you will be doing:</p><ul><li><p>Develop and optimize our iOS applications using Swift, with a focus on performance, reliability and user experience.</p></li><li><p>Contribute to application architecture, technical design and the continued development of our modular codebase.</p></li><li><p>Build prototypes and proof of concepts to explore ideas and validate technical solutions early.</p></li><li><p>Create intuitive user interfaces and experiences tailored to iOS devices.</p></li><li><p>Develop and maintain features that communicate with Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) devices.</p></li><li><p>Troubleshoot production issues, review code and help colleagues make sound implementation decisions.</p></li><li><p>Explore relevant developments in mobile technology, including SwiftUI, and assess how they can improve our applications.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Why Luscii?</h3><p><u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://jobs.luscii.com/life-at-luscii/">Read more</a></u> about working at Luscii and <u><a rel="noopener" target="_blank" href="https://jobs.luscii.com/how-we-work/">how</a></u> we work at Luscii/OMRON. Together, we are working on a mission to create space for care. Freedom, autonomy and ownership are of great importance in this. You are responsible for your own results and work according to the principles of Holacracy.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>Most important benefits</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Salary</strong>: € 4.600 - € 5.900 gross per month (based on 32 hours per week – that’s full-time at Luscii).</p></li><li><p><strong>Remote-first</strong>: Work from anywhere in The Netherlands. We stay connected through monthly in-person team days called <em>Assemblii</em>.</p></li><li><p><strong>Flexible setup</strong>: Create your own ideal workspace. Whatever works best for you - we’ve got you covered here.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3>The ideal candidate…</h3><p>… probably doesn't exist, but if you can tick most of the checkboxes below, please apply! We are looking for somebody who is comfortable in taking ownership and making well-considered decisions independently. You enjoy the autonomy to shape your work and responsibilities, while actively seeking collaboration and alignment with others.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>You know when to step up, when to involve colleagues and when to move forward decisively. Working independently does not mean working in isolation for you. You feel at ease being both a self-starter and a committed team player, contributing to shared goals while taking responsibility for your own domain. You value open communication, transparency, and mutual trust.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><ul><li><p>You have at least 5 years of experience as an iOS or mobile developer.</p></li><li><p>You have a relevant bachelor’s degree in e.g. Computer Science, Computer Engineering or a comparable field, combined with experience working in an Agile environment.</p></li><li><p>You have experience writing unit tests and/or UI tests for mobile applications.</p></li><li><p>You understand object-oriented software design and architectural patterns such as MVVM.</p></li><li><p>You have experience with web services, cloud technologies and APIs, and are comfortable debugging issues involving memory management, multithreading and networking.</p></li><li><p>You are open to working in a Holacratic organization and curious about our way of organizing work, roles, and responsibilities;</p></li><li><p>English is our primary language for all internal communication at Luscii, so you're fluent in that language.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong>Interested? Apply now!</strong></h3><p>Would you like more information? Feel free to contact our recruiter Björn Bogerd via <a rel="noopener" target="_blank" ---------- style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong>What does the recruitment process look like?</strong></h3><p>We organise three interviews for each vacancy. It is an extensive process, but we want to ensure that there is a good fit in regards to a potential collaboration, our culture and our way of working. All interviews are conducted online and the entire procedure is planned in advance to keep momentum.</p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/luscii/remote-ios-developer-utrecht-289501","tags":["Software Development","Remote"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1793298667},{"slug":"remote-senior-financial-analyst-fpa-contractor-netherlands-91709","company_name":"PVcase","title":"Senior Financial Analyst (FP&A) (Contractor)","description":"<p><span style="color:#121317">We are seeking a Senior FP&amp;A Analyst to lead end-to-end financial planning, reporting, and forecasting for operating expenses across the organization. In this role, you will own cost center analysis, drive forecast consolidation, manage systems integrity between TM1 and NetSuite, and serve as a strategic finance business partner to department leaders across the company.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">The ideal candidate brings strong financial modeling expertise, hands-on experience with corporate planning tools, and the confidence to constructively challenge operational teams on budget assumptions while translating complex numbers into actionable business narratives.<br><br>Responsibilities:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Own the FP&amp;A OpEx close—analyzing variances, preparing monthly management reporting packs (P&amp;L, dashboards, board inputs), and partnering with Accounting on accruals and prepayments.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Own planning, trend analysis, and variance commentary for non-people OpEx (software, marketing, T&amp;E, professional services). Track cost efficiency metrics and ensure accurate TM1 mapping.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Lead annual OpEx budget cycles and recurring reforecasts. Build dynamic, driver-based forecasting models and support Long-Range Planning (LRP) scenario modeling.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Consolidate OpEx, workforce, and revenue forecasts into a single defensible group view in TM1. Support the FP&amp;A Director in presenting to the CFO, ELT, and Board.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Act as the strategic finance partner to department heads - translating numbers into actionable insights, constructively challenging spend assumptions, and flagging risks/opportunities.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Ensure TM1 remains the single source of truth vs. NetSuite actuals. Drive reporting automation, refine Google Sheets dashboards, and streamline close/budget cycles.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">5-7+ years in finance with 2–3+ years in FP&amp;A. Experience owning end-to-end close/budget cycles and partnering directly with non-finance stakeholders. </span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Tech, SaaS, or scale-up background strongly preferred.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Advanced Excel/Google Sheets modeling skills. Hands-on experience with corporate planning tools (TM1/Cognos is a strong plus; Anaplan/Adaptive) and ERP systems (NetSuite preferred). Strong grasp of core accounting concepts (accruals, prepayments, opex vs. capex).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Commercial mindset, structured thinking, strong communication skills, and the confidence to challenge budget assumptions constructively.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or related field (ACCA/CIMA/CFA or Master's is a plus). Fluent in English (Lithuanian is an advantage).</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h3 style="text-align:start;"><strong>About us</strong></h3><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#1D1C1D">PVcase is moving solar forward with an alternative to the traditional labor-intensive, time-consuming, error-prone solar project development process. With our sophisticated site selection, PV design, and yield estimation software, you can achieve maximum results in a fraction of the time — to succeed faster, build better, and accelerate the global transition to clean energy. PVcase ends clunky processes and corrupted data to clear the path to a net-zero economy.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#1D1C1D">Whether you use a single product or plug into the entire platform, our end-to-end site selection, design, and yield assessment software makes you faster, precise, and highly productive at every stage of project development. PVcase is a leading choice for solar energy professionals — our platform serves over 1,800 customers in 75+ countries, powering the development of more than 4 TW of projects a year.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3 style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">Get ready to enjoy</span></strong></h3><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Flex benefit package, customizing perks to match your unique style.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Enjoy unlimited remote work or join the vibrant offices in Vilnius, Kaunas, or Barcelona.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Flexible working hours, harmonizing your personal and professional life.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Half-day Summer Fridays.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Full training and onboarding program for a seamless start.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Exclusive work only with international markets.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Considerable &amp; steadily increasing salary, recognizing and rewarding your dedication.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Frequent in-office and after-hours activities with team members.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Participation in international training programs.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Internal transparency with company results and salary system, promoting a culture of trust and collaboration.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Additional paid vacation days, including birthdays, volunteering, and other occasions.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Salary Range:</span></strong></p><ul><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">Lithuania: 45,100 - 60,000 EUR gross/yearly.</span></p></li><li><p style="text-align:start;"><span style="color:#121317">Spain: 37,200 - 50,000 EUR gross/yearly.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Netherlands: 57,600 - 75,000 EUR gross/yearly.</span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><em><span style="color:#000000">Immigration-related employment support, such as visa sponsorship or transfer, is not available for this position.</span></em></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/pvcase/remote-senior-financial-analyst-fpa-contractor-netherlands-91709","tags":["Operations","Remote"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Remote job","created_at":1793298665},{"slug":"business-developer-bdr-utrecht-80845","company_name":"SMARTVÉLO GmbH","title":"Business Developer / BDR (m/f/d)","description":"<p>SMARTVÉLO is a fast-growing company for sustainable e-mobility solutions. We develop e-bikes that are changing everyday city life, and we stand for top quality and excellent service. Become part of this vision!</p><p>As Business Developer (m/f/d), you will build our business in the Netherlands and Belgium from the ground up. You will bring SMARTVÉLO e-bikes to new customers in delivery, logistics, restaurants and franchise chains, set up pilots and turn them into long-term fleet deals. You will be our first person on the ground, with a lot of freedom, short decision paths and direct contact with management.</p><h2>Your tasks</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Generate new business:</strong> You create your own opportunities through cold calling, LinkedIn outreach and visiting stores and branches in person</p></li><li><p><strong>Set up pilots:</strong> You bring new customers on board with pilots and convert them into long-term contracts</p></li><li><p><strong>Consultative selling:</strong> Our product is high-end and priced accordingly. You understand the customer's delivery operation and show why it pays off</p></li><li><p><strong>Target the right segments:</strong> You focus on delivery and last-mile, restaurant chains and franchises, grocery retail and care services</p></li><li><p><strong>Stakeholder management:</strong> You talk with operations as well as management and build lasting relationships</p></li><li><p><strong>Interface to Cologne:</strong> You work closely with our sales team and management in Germany and give feedback from the market</p></li></ul><h2>Your profile</h2><ul><li><p>2-5 years of commercial experience with a real track record in new business (not pure account management)</p></li><li><p>Proven experience with cold outreach: you have booked meetings yourself, by phone or in person, without waiting for inbound leads</p></li><li><p>Affinity with mobility, e-bikes, fleet, delivery, logistics, restaurants or franchise</p></li><li><p>Hunter mentality: entrepreneurial, practical, direct and accountable</p></li><li><p>Comfortable with targets, rejection and ambiguity. Not every process is set in stone with us yet</p></li><li><p>Ambition to grow into a senior role</p></li><li><p>Based in or around Utrecht (or within easy reach of central NL), willing to travel a lot</p></li><li><p>Fluent Dutch, good English (German is a plus)</p></li></ul><h2>What we offer</h2><ul><li><p>€50,000 fixed salary plus uncapped bonus: the more e-bikes you sell, the more you earn</p></li><li><p>Company car for your customer visits</p></li><li><p>Real ownership: you build a new market for SMARTVÉLO from scratch</p></li><li><p>Flexible work from home, with at least one team meeting per week</p></li><li><p>Profitable scale-up from Cologne with strong customers (Flink, Wolt, Domino's) and clear growth plans in DACH and the EU</p></li><li><p>State-of-the-art equipment (iPhone & Lenovo laptop)</p></li><li><p>Regular feedback meetings for your development</p></li></ul><p>You don't just want a job, you want to make a difference? Then you've come to the right place!</p><p>We look forward to meeting you - make it ride!</p><p>Your SMARTVÉLO Team</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/smartvelo-gmbh/business-developer-bdr-utrecht-80845","tags":["Business Development"],"job_types":["Permanent contract (vast contract/arbeidsovereenkomst voor onbepaalde tijd)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Utrecht","created_at":1793289683},{"slug":"remote-senior-finance-manager-amsterdam-89155","company_name":"Global Reporting Initiative","title":"Senior Finance Manager","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><strong><span style="color:#121317">About GRI</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Global Reporting Initiative (GRI) is the independent nonprofit organization that is the architect of the common global language to assess and report on environmental, social, and economic impacts. GRI provides standards, tools, and training that empower organizations of all sizes to create sustainable, long-term value and unlock positive change in the world.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">For over 25 years, GRI has led a global multi-stakeholder process to develop and refine rigorous yet practical approaches to sustainability reporting, which meet the needs of all stakeholders. The  GRI Standards,  the world’s most widely used sustainability reporting standards, provide the building blocks for transparent reporting on impacts.&nbsp; Working at GRI, you will be part of unlocking positive change in the world. &nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><strong><span style="color:#121317">About the role</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">The Senior Manager Finance owns budgeting and financial analysis to support the CFO and budget holders in business decision-making. The role also oversees day-to-day finance operations, financial controls and external reporting, and provides line management and guidance to a finance colleague.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Driving automation and process improvement is a central part of the role, using digital tools and AI where appropriate to streamline workflows, automate reporting and reduce manual work. Initially focused on finance, this remit may expand to other processes across GRI in the longer term.</span></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Responsibilities</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><strong><em><span style="color:#121317">Delivery</span></em></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Own and deliver the budgeting, forecasting and financial planning cycle, providing the CFO with robust analysis, scenario modelling, automated dashboards and clear recommendations, while automating data collection and reporting to reduce manual effort and support business decision-making.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Lead process improvement and automation across finance, using digital tools and AI where appropriate to reduce manual work and improve accuracy, timeliness and efficiency, and extend this to other administrative processes across the organization in the longer term.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Maintain strong financial controls, building automated checks and workflows where possible, and, with support from the finance and grant management teams, manage external reporting including consolidated financial statements (under IFRS for SMEs), tax reporting and donor financial reporting.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Provide line management, guidance and development to a finance colleague, overseeing day-to-day finance operations (including payments, reconciliations and month-end close) and coaching them to streamline and automate routine tasks.</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><strong><em><span style="color:#121317"><br>Engagement</span></em></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Act as a finance business partner to budget holders, providing insight into performance, challenging assumptions and supporting informed resource allocation.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Support the CFO in liaising with external partners, including auditors and banks, coordinating information requests and ensuring timely follow-up.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Communicate financial insights clearly to non-financial colleagues and support adoption of new reporting tools and processes.</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><strong><span style="color:#121317">Requirements</span></strong></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><strong><em><span style="color:#121317">Work experience&nbsp;</span></em></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Holds a degree in Finance (Diploma, Master’s, or higher), preferably complemented by a professional accounting qualification (ACCA, ACA, CIMA or equivalent).</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Brings over 5 years of relevant experience in a similar senior financial role.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Demonstrable experience delivering finance process improvements, automation and reporting tools within budgeting, close and reporting cycles. NGO or grant-funded experience is an advantage, not a requirement.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Proven experience providing line management and guidance to a finance colleague and overseeing day-to-day finance operations, including reviewing transactions and reconciliations and ensuring timely, accurate month-end close and financial reporting. Experience supporting budgeting and forecasting and maintaining robust financial controls.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Experience in managing operational budgets exceeding €10 million.</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0" style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><strong><em><span style="color:#121317">Knowledge and abilities</span></em></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Strong digital finance and financial modelling skills, with hands-on experience using ERP systems, analytics and reporting platforms such as Power BI, and advanced spreadsheet and workflow automation tools. Familiarity with AI tools and their practical application to finance and administration; experience developing AI agents is a strong advantage.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">A practical, improvement-oriented mindset, with the ability to turn business needs into effective finance tools and workflows; experience applying automation or AI tools in finance is an advantage.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Ability to solve problems and complexities spanning different functions and processes.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Is capable of setting clear priorities and ensuring an optimum use of time and resources.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Is accurate, reliable, and knows how to deal with confidential information.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Has strong communication and collaboration skills.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Has excellent written and oral skills in English. Additional languages are a plus.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Ability to work in a dynamic environment where change is ongoing.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Able to work in an international and multi-cultural setting.</span></p></li></ul><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Affinity with the mission GRI.</span></p></li></ul><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><strong><span style="color:#121317">What we offer</span></strong></p><ul class="BulletListStyle3 SCXW246917265 BCX0"><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW246917265 BCX0"><span style="color:#121317">Remote and/or hybrid work (within +/- 2 hour CET; (candidates must have an existing pe